WEBVTT


00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:15.701
<b>@ www.subs4free.com</b>


00:00:26.702 --> 00:00:29.542
<i>The Tesseract has awakened.</i>


00:00:29.542 --> 00:00:30.497
<i>The Tesseract has awakened.</i>


00:00:31.302 --> 00:00:36.057
It is on a little world, a human world.


00:00:36.742 --> 00:00:39.939
They would wield its power,


00:00:40.302 --> 00:00:45.740
but our ally knows its
workings as they never will.


00:00:47.222 --> 00:00:50.180
<i>He is ready to lead</i>


00:00:50.382 --> 00:00:55.582
<i>and our force, our Chitauri, will follow.</i>


00:00:57.143 --> 00:00:59.418
<i>A world will be his.</i>


00:00:59.623 --> 00:01:02.615
<i>The universe, yours.</i>


00:01:02.823 --> 00:01:08.455
<i>And the humans,
what can they do but burn?</i>


00:01:22.103 --> 00:01:23.138
<i>All personnel,</i>


00:01:23.303 --> 00:01:25.498
<i>the evacuation order
has been confirmed.</i>


00:01:56.104 --> 00:01:57.503
How bad is it?


00:01:57.704 --> 00:02:00.855
That's the problem, sir. We don't know.


00:02:04.304 --> 00:02:07.102
Dr Selvig read an energy surge
from the Tesseract four hours ago.


00:02:07.224 --> 00:02:09.021
NASA didn't authorise Selvig
to go to test phase.


00:02:09.224 --> 00:02:11.294
He wasn't testing it.
He wasn't even in the room.


00:02:11.504 --> 00:02:12.459
Spontaneous event.


00:02:12.624 --> 00:02:13.693
It just turned itself on?


00:02:13.904 --> 00:02:14.893
Where are the energy levels now?


00:02:15.104 --> 00:02:17.174
Climbing. When Selvig couldn't
shut it down, we ordered evac.


00:02:17.384 --> 00:02:18.533
How long to get everyone out?


00:02:18.744 --> 00:02:20.018
Campus should be clear
in the next half-hour.


00:02:20.224 --> 00:02:21.418
Do better.


00:02:22.344 --> 00:02:24.221
Sir, evacuation may be futile.


00:02:24.424 --> 00:02:25.743
We should tell them
to go back to sleep?


00:02:25.944 --> 00:02:28.060
If we can't control
the Tesseract's energy,


00:02:28.264 --> 00:02:30.495
there may not be
a minimum safe distance.


00:02:30.625 --> 00:02:31.614
I need you to make sure


00:02:31.745 --> 00:02:33.337
the Phase 2 prototypes
are shipped out.


00:02:33.505 --> 00:02:35.461
Sir, is that really a priority right now?


00:02:35.665 --> 00:02:37.303
Until such time as the world ends,


00:02:37.425 --> 00:02:39.381
we will act as though
it intends to spin on.


00:02:40.305 --> 00:02:41.624
Clear out the tech below.


00:02:41.825 --> 00:02:44.214
Every piece of Phase 2
on a truck and gone.


00:02:44.425 --> 00:02:45.460
Yes, sir.


00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:46.980
With me.


00:02:49.945 --> 00:02:50.900
Talk to me, Doctor.


00:02:52.625 --> 00:02:53.944
Director.


00:02:54.145 --> 00:02:55.737
Is there anything we know for certain?


00:02:55.945 --> 00:02:58.095
The Tesseract is misbehaving.


00:02:58.305 --> 00:03:00.978
- Is that supposed to be funny?
- No, it's not funny at all.


00:03:01.185 --> 00:03:04.541
The Tesseract is not only
active, she's behaving.


00:03:04.745 --> 00:03:05.700
I assume you pulled the plug.


00:03:05.905 --> 00:03:07.543
She's an energy source.


00:03:07.745 --> 00:03:10.657
We turn off the power,
she turns it back on.


00:03:10.865 --> 00:03:11.900
If she reaches peak level...


00:03:12.105 --> 00:03:15.381
We prepared for this, Doctor.
Harnessing energy from space.


00:03:15.585 --> 00:03:16.904
But we don't have the harness.


00:03:17.025 --> 00:03:18.254
My calculations are far from complete.


00:03:18.786 --> 00:03:21.220
And she's throwing off
interference, radiation.


00:03:21.426 --> 00:03:23.064
Nothing harmful,
low levels of gamma radiation.


00:03:23.946 --> 00:03:25.698
That can be harmful.


00:03:25.906 --> 00:03:27.259
Where's Agent Barton?


00:03:27.426 --> 00:03:29.064
The Hawk?


00:03:29.906 --> 00:03:31.862
Up in his nest, as usual.


00:03:33.266 --> 00:03:34.984
<i>Agent Barton, report.</i>


00:03:35.826 --> 00:03:36.941
<i>I gave you this detail</i>


00:03:37.066 --> 00:03:38.579
<i>so you could keep
a close eye on things.</i>


00:03:38.786 --> 00:03:40.105
Well, I see better from a distance.


00:03:40.306 --> 00:03:42.183
Have you seen anything
that might set this thing off?


00:03:42.626 --> 00:03:44.662
Doctor, it's spiking again.


00:03:44.866 --> 00:03:46.185
No one's come or gone.


00:03:46.386 --> 00:03:47.944
And Selvig's clean.


00:03:48.146 --> 00:03:50.341
No contacts, no IMs.


00:03:50.826 --> 00:03:52.544
If there was any tampering,
sir, it wasn't at this end.


00:03:54.386 --> 00:03:55.705
"At this end"?


00:03:55.906 --> 00:03:59.581
Yeah, the Cube is a doorway to
the other end of space, right?


00:04:01.346 --> 00:04:02.574
Doors open from both sides.


00:04:03.306 --> 00:04:04.580
Not yet.


00:05:09.708 --> 00:05:12.700
Sir, please put down the spear.


00:05:50.429 --> 00:05:51.544
You have heart.


00:06:20.869 --> 00:06:22.302
Please don't.


00:06:24.029 --> 00:06:25.178
I still need that.


00:06:25.389 --> 00:06:26.788
This doesn't have to get any messier.


00:06:26.989 --> 00:06:28.138
Of course it does.


00:06:28.349 --> 00:06:30.147
I've come too far for anything else.


00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.703
I am Loki, of Asgard


00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:37.665
and I am burdened with
glorious purpose.


00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:39.223
Loki,


00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:40.938
brother of Thor.


00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:43.505
We have no quarrel with your people.


00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:46.543
An ant has no quarrel with a boot.


00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.702
Are you planning to step on us?


00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:51.988
I come with glad tidings


00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:55.021
of a world made free.


00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:56.345
Free from what?


00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:57.824
Freedom.


00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:00.864
Freedom is life's great lie.


00:07:01.070 --> 00:07:04.346
Once you accept that, in your heart,


00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:10.467
you will know peace.


00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:13.105
Yeah, you say "peace,"


00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:15.062
I kind of think you mean the other thing.


00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:17.660
Sir, Director Fury is stalling.


00:07:17.871 --> 00:07:19.145
This place is about to blow


00:07:19.271 --> 00:07:20.909
and drop a hundred feet of rock on us.


00:07:22.351 --> 00:07:23.340
He means to bury us.


00:07:23.551 --> 00:07:24.620
Like the pharaohs of old.


00:07:24.831 --> 00:07:26.708
He's right. The portal
is collapsing in on itself.


00:07:26.911 --> 00:07:29.027
We've got maybe two minutes
before this goes critical.


00:07:29.391 --> 00:07:30.346
Well, then.


00:07:45.471 --> 00:07:46.506
I need these vehicles.


00:07:50.431 --> 00:07:52.467
- Who's that?
- They didn't tell me.


00:07:55.551 --> 00:07:56.745
<i>Hill!</i>


00:07:57.151 --> 00:07:58.379
Do you copy?


00:07:59.071 --> 00:08:00.345
<i>Barton has turned.</i>


00:08:12.872 --> 00:08:15.591
They have the Tesseract!
Shut them down!


00:08:50.512 --> 00:08:52.629
Okay, let's go. No, leave it. Go!


00:09:08.433 --> 00:09:10.469
We're clear upstairs, sir.
You need to go.


00:10:38.675 --> 00:10:39.949
<i>Director?</i>


00:10:40.275 --> 00:10:41.708
Director Fury, do you copy?


00:10:41.915 --> 00:10:44.110
The Tesseract is with a hostile force.


00:10:44.355 --> 00:10:46.664
I have men down. Hill?


00:10:46.995 --> 00:10:48.792
A lot of men still under.


00:10:48.995 --> 00:10:50.633
I don't know how many survivors.


00:10:50.835 --> 00:10:51.950
<i>Sound a general call.</i>


00:10:52.155 --> 00:10:53.793
I want every living soul
not working rescue


00:10:53.915 --> 00:10:54.870
looking for that briefcase.


00:10:55.075 --> 00:10:56.064
Roger that.


00:10:56.275 --> 00:10:59.426
Coulson, get back to base.
This is a Level Seven.


00:11:00.475 --> 00:11:01.988
<i>As of right now,</i>


00:11:02.195 --> 00:11:03.594
we are at war.


00:11:05.235 --> 00:11:06.463
What do we do?


00:11:41.836 --> 00:11:45.385
This is not how I wanted this evening
to go.


00:11:45.516 --> 00:11:47.074
I know how you wanted this evening
to go.


00:11:47.276 --> 00:11:48.311
Believe me


00:11:48.436 --> 00:11:49.425
this is better.


00:11:50.356 --> 00:11:52.153
Who are you working for?


00:11:52.516 --> 00:11:54.029
Lermentov, yes?


00:11:55.916 --> 00:11:57.315
Does he think


00:11:57.916 --> 00:11:59.634
we have to go through him


00:11:59.916 --> 00:12:01.315
to move our cargo?


00:12:02.517 --> 00:12:06.874
I thought General Solohob
is in charge of the export business.


00:12:07.197 --> 00:12:09.074
Solohob


00:12:09.277 --> 00:12:11.233
a bagman, a front.


00:12:13.597 --> 00:12:17.590
Your outdated information betrays you.


00:12:19.117 --> 00:12:21.756
The famous Black Widow


00:12:23.357 --> 00:12:27.555
and she turns out to be
simply another pretty face.


00:12:28.397 --> 00:12:31.434
You really think I'm pretty?


00:12:33.877 --> 00:12:36.027
Tell Lermentov we don't need him


00:12:36.317 --> 00:12:39.753
to move the tanks.


00:12:40.677 --> 00:12:43.191
Tell him he is out.


00:12:43.597 --> 00:12:45.155
Well...


00:12:47.917 --> 00:12:49.590
...you may have to write it down.


00:12:58.198 --> 00:12:59.597
It's for her.


00:13:02.918 --> 00:13:04.146
You listen carefully


00:13:04.278 --> 00:13:06.746
<i>You're at 1- 14
Silensky Plaza, 3rd floor.</i>


00:13:06.998 --> 00:13:09.034
<i>We have an F-22
exactly eight miles out.</i>


00:13:09.878 --> 00:13:11.755
<i>Put the woman on the phone,
or I will blow up the block</i>


00:13:11.958 --> 00:13:13.914
<i>before you can make the lobby.</i>


00:13:20.118 --> 00:13:22.154
<i>- We need you to come in.
- Are you kidding? I'm working.</i>


00:13:22.358 --> 00:13:23.586
<i>This takes precedence.</i>


00:13:23.798 --> 00:13:25.356
I'm in the middle of an interrogation.


00:13:25.518 --> 00:13:27.236
This moron is giving me everything.


00:13:27.638 --> 00:13:30.152
I don't give everything.


00:13:31.518 --> 00:13:32.837
Look, you can't pull me
out of this right now.


00:13:32.958 --> 00:13:33.913
<i>Natasha...</i>


00:13:35.438 --> 00:13:36.871
Barton's been compromised.


00:13:39.959 --> 00:13:41.711
Let me put you on hold.


00:14:21.759 --> 00:14:22.714
Where is Barton now?


00:14:22.879 --> 00:14:24.312
<i>- We don't know.
- But he's alive?</i>


00:14:24.519 --> 00:14:27.193
We think so. I'll brief you on
everything when you get back.


00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:29.396
But first, we need you to
talk to the big guy.


00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:32.558
Coulson, you know that Stark trusts me
about as far as he can throw me.


00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:36.116
I've got Stark. You get the big guy.


00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:00.795
Who are you?


00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:02.275
Get out!


00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:04.789
There is sickness here!


00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:05.875
You're a doctor.


00:15:07.520 --> 00:15:08.748
My father's not waking up!


00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:10.632
He has a fever and he's moaning


00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:11.795
but his eyes won't open.


00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:12.876
Slow down.


00:15:14.361 --> 00:15:15.396
My father...


00:15:17.681 --> 00:15:18.636
Like them?


00:15:22.481 --> 00:15:23.675
Please.


00:15:49.761 --> 00:15:51.956
You should've got paid
up front, Banner.


00:15:52.161 --> 00:15:53.389
You know, for a man


00:15:53.521 --> 00:15:54.749
who's supposed to be avoiding stress


00:15:54.961 --> 00:15:58.078
you picked a hell of a place to settle.


00:15:59.761 --> 00:16:01.878
Avoiding stress isn't the secret.


00:16:02.082 --> 00:16:04.471
Then what is it? Yoga?


00:16:05.602 --> 00:16:08.639
You brought me to the edge of
the city. Smart.


00:16:09.202 --> 00:16:13.081
I assume the whole place
is surrounded.


00:16:13.522 --> 00:16:14.841
Just you and me.


00:16:16.042 --> 00:16:17.998
And your actress buddy?


00:16:18.202 --> 00:16:20.079
Is she a spy, too?
They start that young?


00:16:20.482 --> 00:16:21.676
I did.


00:16:21.882 --> 00:16:22.871
Who are you?


00:16:23.082 --> 00:16:24.151
Natasha Romanoff.


00:16:27.362 --> 00:16:28.636
Are you here to kill me, Ms Romanoff?


00:16:28.842 --> 00:16:31.436
Because that's not going to
work out for everyone.


00:16:31.642 --> 00:16:33.997
No, of course not. I'm here
on behalf of S.H.I.E.L.D.


00:16:35.682 --> 00:16:37.115
S.H.I.E.L.D.


00:16:38.842 --> 00:16:39.797
How did they find me?


00:16:39.962 --> 00:16:41.520
We never lost you, Doctor.


00:16:41.722 --> 00:16:42.677
We've kept our distance.


00:16:42.882 --> 00:16:44.600
Even helped keep some other
interested parties


00:16:44.762 --> 00:16:45.751
off your scent.


00:16:46.242 --> 00:16:47.197
Why?


00:16:47.322 --> 00:16:49.598
Nick Fury seems to trust you.


00:16:49.803 --> 00:16:51.361
But now we need you to come in.


00:16:52.283 --> 00:16:54.080
What if I say no?


00:16:54.283 --> 00:16:56.319
I'll persuade you.


00:16:58.363 --> 00:17:02.515
And what if the other guy says no?


00:17:03.203 --> 00:17:04.761
You've been more than a year
without an incident.


00:17:04.963 --> 00:17:07.431
I don't think you want to
break that streak.


00:17:09.563 --> 00:17:12.077
Well, I don't every time get what I want.


00:17:13.083 --> 00:17:15.199
Doctor, we're facing a potential
global catastrophe.


00:17:16.003 --> 00:17:18.995
Well, those I actively try to avoid.


00:17:19.323 --> 00:17:21.279
This


00:17:21.483 --> 00:17:23.758
is the Tesseract.


00:17:23.963 --> 00:17:26.636
It has the potential energy
to wipe out the planet.


00:17:29.363 --> 00:17:31.433
What does Fury want me to do,
swallow it?


00:17:31.643 --> 00:17:33.998
He wants you to find it. It's been taken.


00:17:34.803 --> 00:17:38.797
It emits a gamma signature
that's too weak for us to trace.


00:17:39.004 --> 00:17:41.802
There's no one that knows
gamma radiation like you do.


00:17:42.004 --> 00:17:44.677
If there was, that's where I'd be.


00:17:45.244 --> 00:17:47.314
So, Fury isn't after the monster?


00:17:47.524 --> 00:17:48.718
Not that he's told me.


00:17:48.924 --> 00:17:50.994
And he tells you everything?


00:17:51.644 --> 00:17:52.963
Talk to Fury. He needs you on this.


00:17:53.084 --> 00:17:54.073
He needs me in a cage?


00:17:54.204 --> 00:17:55.159
No one's going to put you in a...


00:17:55.324 --> 00:17:56.279
Stop lying to me!


00:18:00.324 --> 00:18:02.838
I'm sorry. That was mean.


00:18:03.764 --> 00:18:05.834
I just wanted to see what you'd do.


00:18:07.004 --> 00:18:09.837
Why don't we do this the easy way


00:18:10.044 --> 00:18:11.238
where you don't use that


00:18:11.444 --> 00:18:15.198
and the other guy
doesn't make a mess.


00:18:15.964 --> 00:18:17.192
Okay?


00:18:18.164 --> 00:18:19.438
Natasha?


00:18:24.885 --> 00:18:25.874
Stand down.


00:18:26.805 --> 00:18:28.284
<i>We're good here.</i>


00:18:30.045 --> 00:18:31.524
"Just you and me."


00:18:33.605 --> 00:18:36.073
<i>This is out of line, Director.</i>


00:18:36.285 --> 00:18:38.594
<i>You're dealing
with forces you can't control.</i>


00:18:39.005 --> 00:18:42.315
You ever been in a war,
Councilman? In a firefight?


00:18:42.525 --> 00:18:45.198
Did you feel
an overabundance of control?


00:18:45.405 --> 00:18:48.636
<i>You're saying that this Asgard
is declaring war on our planet?</i>


00:18:48.765 --> 00:18:51.279
Not Asgard. Loki.


00:18:51.485 --> 00:18:54.158
<i>He can't be working alone.
What about the other one?</i>


00:18:54.285 --> 00:18:55.274
<i>His brother.</i>


00:18:55.405 --> 00:18:57.361
Our intelligence says
Thor is not a hostile


00:18:57.565 --> 00:18:58.520
but he's worlds away.


00:18:58.685 --> 00:19:00.403
We can't depend on him to help, either.


00:19:00.525 --> 00:19:01.480
It's up to us.


00:19:01.605 --> 00:19:04.119
<i>Which is why you
should be focusing on Phase 2.</i>


00:19:04.285 --> 00:19:05.513
<i>It was designed for exactly this...</i>


00:19:05.725 --> 00:19:08.762
Phase 2 isn't ready. Our enemy is.


00:19:09.005 --> 00:19:10.484
We need a response team.


00:19:10.686 --> 00:19:12.881
<i>The Avengers Initiative was shut down.</i>


00:19:13.086 --> 00:19:14.804
This isn't about the Avengers.


00:19:15.006 --> 00:19:16.075
<i>We've seen the list.</i>


00:19:16.286 --> 00:19:18.402
<i>You're running the world's greatest
covert security network</i>


00:19:18.526 --> 00:19:20.084
<i>and you're going to leave
the fate of the human race</i>


00:19:20.246 --> 00:19:21.440
<i>to a handful of freaks.</i>


00:19:21.566 --> 00:19:23.397
I'm not leaving anything to anyone.


00:19:23.606 --> 00:19:25.722
We need a response team.


00:19:25.966 --> 00:19:28.560
These people may be isolated,
unbalanced even


00:19:28.766 --> 00:19:32.759
but I believe with the right push
they can be exactly what we need.


00:19:33.046 --> 00:19:34.274
<i>You believe?</i>


00:19:34.486 --> 00:19:37.922
<i>War isn't won by sentiment, Director.</i>


00:19:38.606 --> 00:19:41.803
No, it's won by soldiers.


00:20:00.647 --> 00:20:02.365
<i>There's not enough time.</i>


00:20:02.567 --> 00:20:04.046
<i>I got to put her in the water!</i>


00:20:09.207 --> 00:20:10.196
<i>You won't be alone.</i>


00:20:10.767 --> 00:20:12.200
<i>Oh, my God.</i>


00:20:12.647 --> 00:20:13.762
<i>This guy is still alive!</i>


00:20:37.527 --> 00:20:39.199
Trouble sleeping?


00:20:40.487 --> 00:20:43.047
I slept for 70 years, sir.
I think I've had my fill.


00:20:44.527 --> 00:20:48.282
Then you should be out,
celebrating, seeing the world.


00:20:53.888 --> 00:20:56.607
When I went under,
the world was at war.


00:20:56.808 --> 00:20:58.560
I wake up, they say we won.


00:20:59.248 --> 00:21:00.727
They didn't say what we lost.


00:21:01.288 --> 00:21:03.518
We've made some mistakes
along the way.


00:21:03.928 --> 00:21:05.520
Some, very recently.


00:21:07.008 --> 00:21:08.157
Are you here with a mission, sir?


00:21:08.288 --> 00:21:09.243
I am.


00:21:09.368 --> 00:21:10.960
Trying to get me back in the world?


00:21:11.448 --> 00:21:13.040
Trying to save it.


00:21:17.528 --> 00:21:19.439
HYDRA's secret weapon.


00:21:19.648 --> 00:21:21.639
Howard Stark fished that
out of the ocean


00:21:21.768 --> 00:21:22.837
when he was looking for you.


00:21:23.368 --> 00:21:24.960
He thought what we think.


00:21:25.208 --> 00:21:29.167
The Tesseract could be the key
to unlimited sustainable energy.


00:21:29.608 --> 00:21:33.283
That's something
the world sorely needs.


00:21:34.729 --> 00:21:35.844
Who took it from you?


00:21:36.049 --> 00:21:37.402
He's called Loki.


00:21:37.609 --> 00:21:40.123
He's not from around here.


00:21:40.569 --> 00:21:42.560
There's a lot we'll have to
bring you up to speed on


00:21:42.689 --> 00:21:43.838
if you're in.


00:21:44.729 --> 00:21:46.685
The world has gotten even stranger


00:21:46.809 --> 00:21:47.844
than you already know.


00:21:48.329 --> 00:21:50.797
At this point, I doubt
anything would surprise me.


00:21:51.409 --> 00:21:53.001
Ten bucks says you're wrong.


00:21:54.689 --> 00:21:56.008
There's a debriefing packet


00:21:56.129 --> 00:21:58.404
waiting for you back at your apartment.


00:22:00.689 --> 00:22:02.520
Is there anything you can
tell us about the Tesseract


00:22:02.649 --> 00:22:03.798
that we ought to know now?


00:22:04.089 --> 00:22:06.284
You should have left it in the ocean.


00:22:37.690 --> 00:22:40.443
<i>Good to go on this end.
The rest is up to you.</i>


00:22:40.650 --> 00:22:41.924
<i>You disconnected
the transmission lines?</i>


00:22:42.050 --> 00:22:43.005
<i>Are we off the grid?</i>


00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:45.200
Stark Tower is about to become
a beacon


00:22:45.370 --> 00:22:46.769
of self-sustaining clean energy.


00:22:46.890 --> 00:22:48.846
<i>Well, assuming
the arc reactor takes over</i>


00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:50.119
<i>and it actually works.</i>


00:22:50.490 --> 00:22:51.718
<i>I assume.</i>


00:22:52.210 --> 00:22:53.165
Light her up.


00:22:58.490 --> 00:22:59.445
<i>How does it look?</i>


00:22:59.610 --> 00:23:02.170
Like Christmas, but with more me.


00:23:02.370 --> 00:23:04.042
<i>We've got to go wider on
the public awareness campaign.</i>


00:23:04.250 --> 00:23:05.239
<i>You need to do some press.</i>


00:23:05.850 --> 00:23:06.805
<i>I'm in DC tomorrow,</i>


00:23:06.970 --> 00:23:08.403
<i>I'm working on the zoning
for the next three buildings.</i>


00:23:08.570 --> 00:23:10.687
<i>Pepper, you're killing me.
The moment, remember?</i>


00:23:10.891 --> 00:23:11.880
<i>Enjoy the moment.</i>


00:23:12.091 --> 00:23:13.206
<i>Get in here and I will.</i>


00:23:16.411 --> 00:23:19.209
<i>Sir, Agent Coulson of
S.H.I.E.L.D. Is on the line.</i>


00:23:19.771 --> 00:23:20.726
<i>I'm not in.</i>


00:23:21.371 --> 00:23:22.599
I'm actually out.


00:23:29.531 --> 00:23:32.045
<i>Sir, I'm afraid he's insisting.</i>


00:23:32.251 --> 00:23:34.890
Grow a spine, Jarvis. I got a date.


00:23:39.251 --> 00:23:42.084
Levels are holding steady, I think.


00:23:42.291 --> 00:23:44.361
Of course they are.
I was directly involved.


00:23:44.571 --> 00:23:45.686
Which brings me to my next question.


00:23:45.851 --> 00:23:47.728
How does it feel to be a genius?


00:23:47.931 --> 00:23:50.081
Well, I really wouldn't know,
now would I?


00:23:50.291 --> 00:23:54.603
What do you mean?
All this came from you.


00:23:54.811 --> 00:23:58.282
No, all this came from that.


00:23:58.492 --> 00:24:00.687
Give yourself some credit. Please.


00:24:00.892 --> 00:24:02.610
Stark Tower is your baby.


00:24:02.812 --> 00:24:05.087
Give yourself 12% of the credit.


00:24:05.532 --> 00:24:06.601
12%?


00:24:06.732 --> 00:24:07.801
An argument can be made for 15.


00:24:07.932 --> 00:24:09.445
12%? My baby?


00:24:09.652 --> 00:24:11.165
Well, I did do all the heavy lifting.


00:24:11.292 --> 00:24:13.089
Literally, I lifted the heavy things.


00:24:13.332 --> 00:24:15.482
And, sorry, but the security snafu?


00:24:15.612 --> 00:24:17.011
That was on you.


00:24:17.172 --> 00:24:19.163
- My private elevator...
- You mean our elevator?


00:24:19.372 --> 00:24:21.932
...it was teeming with sweaty workmen.


00:24:22.132 --> 00:24:24.362
I'm going to pay for that
comment about percentages


00:24:24.572 --> 00:24:26.449
in some subtle way later, aren't I?


00:24:26.892 --> 00:24:28.041
It's not going to be that subtle.


00:24:28.252 --> 00:24:29.480
I'll tell you what.


00:24:29.692 --> 00:24:32.047
The next building is gonna
say "Potts" on the tower.


00:24:32.252 --> 00:24:33.571
On the lease.


00:24:34.452 --> 00:24:36.488
Call your mom. Can you bunk over?


00:24:36.692 --> 00:24:37.886
<i>Sir, the telephone.</i>


00:24:38.092 --> 00:24:40.367
<i>I'm afraid my protocols
are being overridden.</i>


00:24:40.572 --> 00:24:42.449
<i>Mr Stark, we need to talk.</i>


00:24:42.732 --> 00:24:44.963
You have reached the life
model decoy of Tony Stark.


00:24:45.213 --> 00:24:47.090
<i>- Please leave a message.
- This is urgent.</i>


00:24:47.293 --> 00:24:49.011
Then leave it urgently.


00:24:50.493 --> 00:24:51.562
Security breach. It's on you.


00:24:51.773 --> 00:24:54.367
- Mr Stark.
- Phil! Come in.


00:24:54.533 --> 00:24:55.488
"Phil"?


00:24:55.613 --> 00:24:56.602
I can't stay.


00:24:56.813 --> 00:24:57.962
His first name is "Agent."


00:24:58.173 --> 00:24:59.731
Come on in. We're celebrating.


00:24:59.933 --> 00:25:01.651
Which is why he can't stay.


00:25:01.853 --> 00:25:03.730
We need you to look this over
as soon as possible.


00:25:03.933 --> 00:25:04.922
I don't like being handed things.


00:25:05.133 --> 00:25:06.532
That's fine, because
I love to be handed things.


00:25:06.733 --> 00:25:08.007
So, let's trade.


00:25:09.333 --> 00:25:10.766
Thank you.


00:25:11.933 --> 00:25:14.049
Official consulting hours
are between 8 and 5


00:25:14.173 --> 00:25:15.128
every other Thursday.


00:25:15.293 --> 00:25:16.248
This isn't a consultation.


00:25:16.373 --> 00:25:17.567
Is this about the Avengers?


00:25:17.973 --> 00:25:19.725
Which I know nothing about.


00:25:19.933 --> 00:25:22.367
The Avengers Initiative
was scrapped, I thought.


00:25:22.573 --> 00:25:23.892
And I didn't even qualify.


00:25:24.093 --> 00:25:25.048
I didn't know that either.


00:25:25.213 --> 00:25:27.966
Apparently I'm volatile, self-obsessed,


00:25:28.093 --> 00:25:29.287
don't play well with others.


00:25:29.573 --> 00:25:30.528
That I did know.


00:25:30.653 --> 00:25:32.212
This isn't about personality
profiles any more.


00:25:32.374 --> 00:25:34.604
Whatever. Ms Potts, got a second?


00:25:34.814 --> 00:25:35.769
Half a mo.


00:25:40.854 --> 00:25:43.084
You know, I thought we were
having a moment.


00:25:43.294 --> 00:25:44.807
I was having 12% of a moment.


00:25:45.974 --> 00:25:48.329
This seems serious.
Phil's pretty shaken.


00:25:48.534 --> 00:25:50.411
How would you know if it's...
Why is he "Phil"?


00:25:50.614 --> 00:25:52.286
What is all this?


00:25:52.494 --> 00:25:53.973
This is


00:25:54.654 --> 00:25:55.609
this.


00:26:02.654 --> 00:26:03.973
I'm going to take the jet to DC tonight.


00:26:04.094 --> 00:26:05.083
Tomorrow.


00:26:05.214 --> 00:26:07.409
You have homework.
You have a lot of homework.


00:26:07.614 --> 00:26:09.252
Well, what if I didn't?


00:26:09.854 --> 00:26:11.173
- Lf you didn't?
- Yeah.


00:26:11.374 --> 00:26:13.444
You mean when you've finished?


00:26:14.494 --> 00:26:17.645
Well, then...


00:26:22.655 --> 00:26:23.883
Square deal. Fly safe.


00:26:27.935 --> 00:26:29.004
Work hard.


00:26:31.775 --> 00:26:33.447
So, any chance
you're driving by LaGuardia?


00:26:33.655 --> 00:26:36.294
- I can drop you.
- Fantastic.


00:26:36.415 --> 00:26:37.370
I want to hear


00:26:37.495 --> 00:26:39.087
about the cellist. Is that still a thing?


00:26:39.295 --> 00:26:40.364
She moved back to Portland.


00:26:40.575 --> 00:26:43.567
What? Boo!


00:26:51.295 --> 00:26:53.604
We're about 40 minutes
out from home base, sir.


00:26:57.175 --> 00:27:00.690
So, this Dr Banner was trying
to replicate the serum they used on me?


00:27:00.895 --> 00:27:02.374
A lot of people were.


00:27:02.575 --> 00:27:04.133
You were the world's first superhero.


00:27:04.815 --> 00:27:07.410
Banner thought gamma radiation
might hold the key to unlocking


00:27:07.576 --> 00:27:08.850
Erskine's original formula.


00:27:09.856 --> 00:27:11.175
Didn't really go his way, did it?


00:27:11.576 --> 00:27:12.975
Not so much.


00:27:13.176 --> 00:27:15.895
When he's not that thing, though,
the guy's like a Stephen Hawking.


00:27:17.856 --> 00:27:20.290
He's like a smart person.


00:27:22.336 --> 00:27:23.405
I gotta say,


00:27:23.736 --> 00:27:26.045
it's an honour to meet you officially.


00:27:26.776 --> 00:27:28.209
I've sort of met you. I mean,


00:27:28.376 --> 00:27:30.094
I watched you while you were sleeping.


00:27:31.856 --> 00:27:33.972
I mean, I was present


00:27:34.176 --> 00:27:37.327
while you were
unconscious from the ice.


00:27:37.536 --> 00:27:39.731
You know, it's really just a huge honour


00:27:39.856 --> 00:27:41.733
to have you on board this...


00:27:42.096 --> 00:27:43.893
I hope I'm the man for the job.


00:27:44.096 --> 00:27:46.849
Oh, you are. Absolutely.


00:27:47.056 --> 00:27:49.809
We made some modifications
to the uniform.


00:27:50.016 --> 00:27:51.449
I had a little design input.


00:27:51.656 --> 00:27:52.850
The uniform?


00:27:53.056 --> 00:27:55.446
Aren't the stars and stripes a little


00:27:56.577 --> 00:27:57.851
old-fashioned?


00:27:58.657 --> 00:28:00.727
With everything that's happening


00:28:00.937 --> 00:28:02.495
and the things that are about
to come to light,


00:28:03.337 --> 00:28:06.647
people might just need
a little old-fashioned.


00:28:37.857 --> 00:28:40.690
The Chitauri grow restless.


00:28:40.897 --> 00:28:42.536
Let them gird themselves.


00:28:42.658 --> 00:28:44.376
I will lead them in the glorious battle.


00:28:44.578 --> 00:28:45.693
Battle?


00:28:46.498 --> 00:28:49.456
Against the meagre might of Earth?


00:28:49.658 --> 00:28:52.377
Glorious, not lengthy.


00:28:52.578 --> 00:28:56.207
If your force
is as formidable as you claim.


00:28:56.418 --> 00:28:58.807
You question us?


00:28:59.018 --> 00:29:01.054
You question him,


00:29:01.218 --> 00:29:03.573
he who put the sceptre in your hand?


00:29:03.778 --> 00:29:06.576
Who gave you ancient knowledge
and new purpose


00:29:06.778 --> 00:29:09.531
when you were cast out, defeated?


00:29:09.738 --> 00:29:11.535
I was a king!


00:29:11.738 --> 00:29:13.854
The rightful king of Asgard,


00:29:14.338 --> 00:29:15.293
betrayed.


00:29:15.938 --> 00:29:18.452
Your ambition is little


00:29:18.658 --> 00:29:21.297
and born of childish need.


00:29:21.498 --> 00:29:23.409
We look beyond the Earth


00:29:23.618 --> 00:29:26.451
to the greater worlds
the Tesseract will unveil.


00:29:26.898 --> 00:29:28.251
You don't have the Tesseract yet.


00:29:30.939 --> 00:29:31.894
I don't threaten.


00:29:33.379 --> 00:29:35.847
But until I open the doors,


00:29:36.059 --> 00:29:39.529
until your force is mine to command,


00:29:40.259 --> 00:29:41.977
you are but words.


00:29:42.179 --> 00:29:45.967
You will have your war, Asgardian.


00:29:47.699 --> 00:29:49.610
If you fail,


00:29:50.579 --> 00:29:54.777
if the Tesseract is kept from us,


00:29:54.979 --> 00:29:59.177
there will be no realm, no barren moon,


00:29:59.379 --> 00:30:02.530
no crevice where he cannot find you.


00:30:04.059 --> 00:30:06.698
You think you know pain?


00:30:06.899 --> 00:30:12.337
He will make you long
for something sweet as pain.


00:30:40.340 --> 00:30:41.329
Stow the captain's gear.


00:30:41.460 --> 00:30:42.415
Yes, sir.


00:30:43.900 --> 00:30:46.892
Agent Romanoff, Captain Rogers.


00:30:47.100 --> 00:30:48.328
- Ma'am.
- Hi.


00:30:48.500 --> 00:30:49.455
They need you on the bridge.


00:30:49.580 --> 00:30:51.013
They're starting the face-trace.


00:30:51.220 --> 00:30:52.255
See you there.


00:30:53.940 --> 00:30:57.899
It was quite the buzz around here,
finding you in the ice.


00:30:58.180 --> 00:31:00.648
I thought Coulson was gonna swoon.


00:31:00.860 --> 00:31:03.613
Did he ask you to sign
his Captain America trading cards yet?


00:31:03.820 --> 00:31:04.969
Trading cards?


00:31:05.181 --> 00:31:07.251
They're vintage. He's very proud.


00:31:08.941 --> 00:31:10.169
Dr Banner.


00:31:12.101 --> 00:31:13.329
Yeah, hi.


00:31:13.861 --> 00:31:15.010
They told me you would be coming.


00:31:15.221 --> 00:31:16.449
Word is, you can find the Cube.


00:31:17.461 --> 00:31:19.258
Is that the only word on me?


00:31:19.661 --> 00:31:20.776
Only word I care about.


00:31:23.261 --> 00:31:25.741
It must be strange for you, all of this.


00:31:26.421 --> 00:31:28.981
Well, this is actually kind of familiar.


00:31:29.181 --> 00:31:31.649
Gentlemen, you might want
to step inside in a minute.


00:31:31.861 --> 00:31:34.500
It's going to get a little hard to breathe.


00:31:35.701 --> 00:31:37.180
<i>Flight crew, secure the deck.</i>


00:31:41.501 --> 00:31:43.014
Is this a submarine?


00:31:43.541 --> 00:31:44.496
Really?


00:31:44.621 --> 00:31:48.216
They want me in a submerged,
pressurised, metal container?


00:32:13.542 --> 00:32:15.817
No, no, this is much worse.


00:32:44.423 --> 00:32:47.017
Hover power check complete.
Position cyclic.


00:32:47.223 --> 00:32:49.532
Increase collective to 8.0%.


00:32:54.423 --> 00:32:56.618
Preparing for maximum
performance takeoff.


00:32:56.743 --> 00:32:58.176
Increase output to capacity.


00:32:58.343 --> 00:33:00.379
Power plant performing at capacity.


00:33:00.583 --> 00:33:01.982
We are clear.


00:33:02.183 --> 00:33:03.616
All engines operating.


00:33:03.823 --> 00:33:08.260
S.H.I.E.L.D. Emergency
Protocol 193.6 in effect.


00:33:08.503 --> 00:33:10.937
- We are at level, sir.
- Good.


00:33:11.303 --> 00:33:12.258
Let's vanish.


00:33:12.463 --> 00:33:14.772
Engage retro-reflection panels.


00:33:29.904 --> 00:33:31.019
Reflection panels engaged.


00:33:31.624 --> 00:33:32.943
Gentlemen.


00:33:44.784 --> 00:33:45.853
Doctor, thank you for coming.


00:33:47.784 --> 00:33:49.581
Thanks for asking nicely.


00:33:49.784 --> 00:33:52.298
So, how long am I staying?


00:33:52.504 --> 00:33:54.222
Once we get our hands on
the Tesseract,


00:33:54.344 --> 00:33:55.493
you're in the wind.


00:33:55.624 --> 00:33:57.376
Where are you with that?


00:33:57.584 --> 00:33:59.256
We're sweeping every
wirelessly accessible


00:33:59.384 --> 00:34:00.339
camera on the planet.


00:34:00.904 --> 00:34:02.622
Cell phones, laptops...


00:34:03.144 --> 00:34:06.295
If it's connected to a satellite,
it's eyes and ears for us.


00:34:06.504 --> 00:34:07.698
That's still not gonna find them in time.


00:34:07.904 --> 00:34:08.859
You have to narrow your field.


00:34:09.064 --> 00:34:10.941
How many spectrometers
do you have access to?


00:34:11.144 --> 00:34:12.702
- How many are there?
- Call every lab you know.


00:34:12.904 --> 00:34:14.542
Tell them to put
the spectrometers on the roof


00:34:14.664 --> 00:34:16.064
and calibrate them for gamma rays.


00:34:16.265 --> 00:34:19.337
I'll rough out a tracking algorithm,
basic cluster recognition.


00:34:19.625 --> 00:34:21.934
At least we could rule out a few places.


00:34:22.185 --> 00:34:23.903
Do you have somewhere
for me to work?


00:34:24.145 --> 00:34:25.214
Agent Romanoff,


00:34:25.385 --> 00:34:27.535
could you show Dr Banner
to his laboratory, please?


00:34:28.625 --> 00:34:30.775
You're gonna love it, Doc.
We got all the toys.


00:34:31.305 --> 00:34:33.023
Put it over there.


00:34:34.945 --> 00:34:36.981
Where did you find all these people?


00:34:37.185 --> 00:34:40.018
S.H.I.E.L.D. Has no shortage
of enemies, Doctor.


00:34:40.465 --> 00:34:41.500
Is this the stuff you need?


00:34:41.665 --> 00:34:42.620
Yeah, iridium.


00:34:42.785 --> 00:34:45.299
It's found in meteorites.
It forms anti-protons.


00:34:45.505 --> 00:34:47.063
It's very hard to get hold of.


00:34:47.265 --> 00:34:48.744
Especially if S.H.I.E.L.D.
Knows you need it.


00:34:48.945 --> 00:34:50.264
Well, I didn't know.


00:34:50.465 --> 00:34:51.614
Hey!


00:34:51.825 --> 00:34:54.020
The Tesseract has shown me so much.


00:34:54.465 --> 00:34:56.296
It's more than knowledge. It's truth.


00:34:56.425 --> 00:34:57.380
I know.


00:34:58.185 --> 00:35:00.016
What did it show you, Agent Barton?


00:35:00.945 --> 00:35:02.298
My next target.


00:35:02.465 --> 00:35:03.421
Tell me what you need.


00:35:06.786 --> 00:35:08.538
I need a distraction.


00:35:09.426 --> 00:35:10.779
And an eyeball.


00:35:17.266 --> 00:35:19.700
I mean, if it's not too much trouble.


00:35:19.906 --> 00:35:20.895
No, no. It's fine.


00:35:23.826 --> 00:35:25.339
It's a vintage set.


00:35:25.546 --> 00:35:27.741
It took me a couple of years
to collect them all.


00:35:30.186 --> 00:35:31.221
Near mint.


00:35:31.426 --> 00:35:32.745
Slight foxing around the edges, but...


00:35:32.946 --> 00:35:35.460
We got a hit. A 67% match.


00:35:35.946 --> 00:35:37.504
Wait. Cross match, 79%.


00:35:38.466 --> 00:35:39.421
Location?


00:35:39.586 --> 00:35:42.498
Stuttgart, Germany. 28 Königstrasse.


00:35:42.706 --> 00:35:43.900
He's not exactly hiding.


00:35:44.106 --> 00:35:45.175
Captain,


00:35:45.506 --> 00:35:46.461
you're up.


00:38:15.630 --> 00:38:16.699
Kneel before me.


00:38:20.990 --> 00:38:22.218
I said


00:38:24.230 --> 00:38:26.300
kneel!


00:38:35.230 --> 00:38:38.461
Is not this simpler?


00:38:39.950 --> 00:38:43.022
Is this not your natural state?


00:38:45.230 --> 00:38:48.302
It's the unspoken truth of humanity,


00:38:48.510 --> 00:38:50.785
that you crave subjugation.


00:38:51.310 --> 00:38:54.939
The bright lure of freedom
diminishes your life's joy


00:38:55.150 --> 00:38:57.618
in a mad scramble for power,


00:38:59.390 --> 00:39:00.709
for identity.


00:39:02.311 --> 00:39:05.508
You were made to be ruled.


00:39:06.111 --> 00:39:07.669
In the end,


00:39:07.911 --> 00:39:10.106
you will always kneel.


00:39:17.191 --> 00:39:19.068
Not to men like you.


00:39:20.071 --> 00:39:21.902
There are no men like me.


00:39:22.751 --> 00:39:25.504
There are always men like you.


00:39:26.751 --> 00:39:28.503
Look to your elder, people.


00:39:30.631 --> 00:39:31.984
Let him be an example.


00:39:38.511 --> 00:39:40.979
You know, the last time
I was in Germany,


00:39:41.191 --> 00:39:44.228
and saw a man standing
above everybody else,


00:39:44.431 --> 00:39:45.830
we ended up disagreeing.


00:39:46.031 --> 00:39:47.908
The soldier.


00:39:49.872 --> 00:39:51.066
The man out of time.


00:39:51.632 --> 00:39:52.826
I'm not the one who's out of time.


00:39:56.192 --> 00:39:58.626
<i>Loki, drop the weapon
and stand down.</i>


00:40:18.152 --> 00:40:19.665
Kneel.


00:40:19.792 --> 00:40:21.145
Not today!


00:40:23.152 --> 00:40:24.380
The guy's all over the place.


00:40:27.752 --> 00:40:29.982
<i>Agent Romanoff. You miss me?</i>


00:40:46.033 --> 00:40:47.433
<i>Make your move, Reindeer Games.</i>


00:40:47.433 --> 00:40:48.024
<i>Make your move, Reindeer Games.</i>


00:40:55.753 --> 00:40:57.152
<i>Good move.</i>


00:40:58.593 --> 00:40:59.821
Mr Stark.


00:41:00.473 --> 00:41:01.588
<i>Captain.</i>


00:41:08.513 --> 00:41:10.071
<i>Is he saying anything?</i>


00:41:10.273 --> 00:41:11.467
Not a word.


00:41:11.753 --> 00:41:13.584
<i>Just get him here. We're low on time.</i>


00:41:16.513 --> 00:41:17.468
I don't like it.


00:41:17.833 --> 00:41:19.710
What, Rock of Ages
giving up so easily?


00:41:19.913 --> 00:41:21.505
I don't remember it being that easy.


00:41:21.673 --> 00:41:23.072
This guy packs a wallop.


00:41:23.273 --> 00:41:26.710
Still, you are pretty spry
for an older fellow.


00:41:27.714 --> 00:41:29.227
What's your thing, Pilates?


00:41:29.394 --> 00:41:30.349
What?


00:41:30.514 --> 00:41:31.469
It's like calisthenics.


00:41:31.594 --> 00:41:33.550
You might have missed
a couple of things


00:41:33.754 --> 00:41:35.312
doing time as a Capsicle.


00:41:37.154 --> 00:41:38.667
Fury didn't tell me
he was calling you in.


00:41:38.874 --> 00:41:41.627
Yeah, there's a lot of things
Fury doesn't tell you.


00:41:41.994 --> 00:41:43.507
Where's this coming from?


00:41:47.434 --> 00:41:49.902
What's the matter? Are you
scared of a little lightning?


00:41:50.314 --> 00:41:52.509
I'm not overly fond of what follows.


00:42:09.594 --> 00:42:10.709
What are you doing?


00:42:23.115 --> 00:42:24.514
<i>And now there's that guy.</i>


00:42:24.715 --> 00:42:26.387
Another Asgardian?


00:42:26.595 --> 00:42:28.347
<i>- That guy's a friendly?
- Doesn't matter.</i>


00:42:28.555 --> 00:42:31.023
<i>If he frees Loki or kills him,
the Tesseract's lost.</i>


00:42:31.235 --> 00:42:32.987
Stark, we need a plan of attack!


00:42:33.195 --> 00:42:35.390
<i>I have a plan. Attack.</i>


00:42:41.155 --> 00:42:42.873
I'd sit this one out, Cap.


00:42:43.075 --> 00:42:44.030
I don't see how I can.


00:42:44.235 --> 00:42:46.749
These guys come from legend.
They're basically gods.


00:42:47.195 --> 00:42:48.423
There's only one God, ma'am.


00:42:48.555 --> 00:42:50.830
And I'm pretty sure
he doesn't dress like that.


00:43:05.676 --> 00:43:06.995
Where is the Tesseract?


00:43:07.196 --> 00:43:08.424
I missed you, too.


00:43:08.636 --> 00:43:10.236
Do I look to be in a gaming mood?


00:43:10.916 --> 00:43:12.235
You should thank me.


00:43:12.676 --> 00:43:14.632
With the Bifrost gone,
how much dark energy


00:43:14.836 --> 00:43:17.475
did the Allfather have to
muster to conjure you here


00:43:17.676 --> 00:43:18.995
to your precious Earth?


00:43:22.956 --> 00:43:24.184
I thought you dead.


00:43:25.756 --> 00:43:27.109
Did you mourn?


00:43:27.556 --> 00:43:29.274
We all did. Our father...


00:43:29.596 --> 00:43:32.394
Your father.


00:43:34.196 --> 00:43:36.949
He did tell you
my true parentage, did he not?


00:43:39.396 --> 00:43:41.546
We were raised together.


00:43:41.756 --> 00:43:44.270
We played together,
we fought together.


00:43:44.756 --> 00:43:45.905
Do you remember none of that?


00:43:46.116 --> 00:43:47.994
I remember a shadow.


00:43:49.437 --> 00:43:52.349
Living in the shade of your greatness.


00:43:53.037 --> 00:43:55.551
I remember you tossing me
into an abyss.


00:43:55.677 --> 00:43:57.588
I, who was, and should be, king!


00:43:57.797 --> 00:43:59.788
So you take the world I love
as a recompense


00:43:59.917 --> 00:44:01.669
for your imagined slights?


00:44:01.877 --> 00:44:04.835
No. The Earth is under
my protection, Loki.


00:44:06.197 --> 00:44:09.587
And you're doing
a marvellous job with that.


00:44:10.037 --> 00:44:11.914
The humans slaughter
each other in droves


00:44:12.037 --> 00:44:13.755
while you idly fret.


00:44:13.957 --> 00:44:16.027
I mean to rule them,
as why should I not?


00:44:16.237 --> 00:44:17.716
You think yourself above them?


00:44:18.757 --> 00:44:19.712
Well, yes.


00:44:19.917 --> 00:44:22.272
Then you miss the truth
of ruling, brother.


00:44:23.077 --> 00:44:24.396
A throne would suit you ill.


00:44:29.397 --> 00:44:32.036
I've seen worlds
you've never known about!


00:44:32.237 --> 00:44:36.231
I have grown, Odinson, in my exile.


00:44:36.598 --> 00:44:38.475
I have seen the true power
of the Tesseract,


00:44:38.598 --> 00:44:39.633
and when I wield it...


00:44:39.838 --> 00:44:41.510
Who showed you this power?


00:44:42.638 --> 00:44:43.912
Who controls the would-be king?


00:44:44.118 --> 00:44:45.836
- I am a king!
- Not here!


00:44:46.038 --> 00:44:47.266
You give up the Tesseract!


00:44:47.398 --> 00:44:49.832
You give up this poisonous dream!


00:44:52.438 --> 00:44:53.757
You come home.


00:44:58.518 --> 00:44:59.587
I don't have it.


00:45:01.598 --> 00:45:03.316
You need the Cube to bring me home.


00:45:03.438 --> 00:45:05.668
But I've sent it off, I know not where.


00:45:06.758 --> 00:45:08.510
You listen well, brother.


00:45:10.398 --> 00:45:11.547
I'm listening.


00:45:20.318 --> 00:45:21.910
Do not touch me again.


00:45:22.118 --> 00:45:23.632
Then don't take my stuff.


00:45:23.839 --> 00:45:25.989
You have no idea
what you're dealing with.


00:45:27.799 --> 00:45:28.754
Shakespeare in the Park?


00:45:30.079 --> 00:45:33.071
Doth Mother know
you wear-eth her drapes?


00:45:33.319 --> 00:45:35.958
This is beyond you, metal man.


00:45:36.159 --> 00:45:38.195
Loki will face Asgardian justice.


00:45:38.399 --> 00:45:41.630
He gives up the Cube,
he's all yours. Until then,


00:45:41.999 --> 00:45:43.193
<i>stay out of the way.</i>


00:45:44.679 --> 00:45:46.237
<i>Tourist.</i>


00:45:51.399 --> 00:45:52.388
Okay.


00:46:20.960 --> 00:46:23.758
Power at 400% capacity.


00:46:23.960 --> 00:46:25.439
How about that?


00:47:23.281 --> 00:47:24.430
Hey!


00:47:26.881 --> 00:47:28.030
That's enough.


00:47:31.761 --> 00:47:33.399
Now, I don't know
what you plan on doing here.


00:47:33.601 --> 00:47:35.796
I've come here to put an end
to Loki's schemes.


00:47:36.001 --> 00:47:38.435
Then prove it. Put that hammer down.


00:47:38.561 --> 00:47:39.516
Yeah... No.


00:47:39.761 --> 00:47:41.160
<i>Bad call. He loves his hammer.</i>


00:47:42.681 --> 00:47:44.831
You want me to put the hammer down?


00:48:11.082 --> 00:48:12.674
Are we done, here?


00:48:58.603 --> 00:49:01.436
In case it's unclear,


00:49:02.123 --> 00:49:03.841
if you try to escape,


00:49:04.883 --> 00:49:07.078
if you so much as scratch that glass,


00:49:16.283 --> 00:49:20.071
it's 30,000 feet straight down
in a steel trap.


00:49:20.604 --> 00:49:22.640
You get how that works?


00:49:24.604 --> 00:49:27.118
Ant, boot.


00:49:30.324 --> 00:49:31.996
It's an impressive cage.


00:49:32.884 --> 00:49:35.398
Not built, I think, for me.


00:49:35.764 --> 00:49:38.073
Built for something
a lot stronger than you.


00:49:38.284 --> 00:49:40.081
Oh, I've heard.


00:49:41.044 --> 00:49:42.159
<i>A mindless beast.</i>


00:49:43.124 --> 00:49:44.682
<i>Makes play he's still a man.</i>


00:49:45.724 --> 00:49:47.874
<i>How desperate are you,</i>


00:49:48.084 --> 00:49:51.042
<i>that you call on such
lost creatures to defend you?</i>


00:49:51.244 --> 00:49:53.474
<i>How desperate am I?</i>


00:49:53.684 --> 00:49:55.402
You threaten my world with war.


00:49:55.604 --> 00:49:57.640
You steal a force
you can't hope to control.


00:49:57.844 --> 00:50:01.473
You talk about peace,
and you kill because it's fun.


00:50:01.684 --> 00:50:04.562
You have made me very desperate.


00:50:04.764 --> 00:50:06.595
You might not be glad that you did.


00:50:09.725 --> 00:50:12.876
It burns you to have come so close.


00:50:14.285 --> 00:50:16.879
To have the Tesseract, to have power,


00:50:17.645 --> 00:50:19.761
unlimited power.


00:50:19.965 --> 00:50:21.842
And for what?


00:50:23.445 --> 00:50:24.125
A warm light for all mankind to share.


00:50:24.125 --> 00:50:27.083
A warm light for all mankind to share.


00:50:27.325 --> 00:50:30.442
And then to be reminded
what real power is.


00:50:34.365 --> 00:50:38.483
Well, let me know if "real power"
wants a magazine or something.


00:50:46.485 --> 00:50:47.884
He really grows on you, doesn't he?


00:50:48.085 --> 00:50:49.916
Loki's gonna drag this out.


00:50:50.125 --> 00:50:53.435
So, Thor, what's his play?


00:50:53.645 --> 00:50:56.080
He has an army called the Chitauri.


00:50:56.286 --> 00:50:59.084
They're not of Asgard,
nor any world known.


00:50:59.486 --> 00:51:01.477
He means to lead them
against your people.


00:51:01.686 --> 00:51:03.199
They will win him the Earth,


00:51:03.326 --> 00:51:05.044
in return, I suspect, for the Tesseract.


00:51:05.246 --> 00:51:06.918
An army


00:51:07.126 --> 00:51:08.718
from outer space.


00:51:08.926 --> 00:51:11.235
So, he's building another portal.


00:51:11.446 --> 00:51:12.720
That's what he needs Erik Selvig for.


00:51:12.846 --> 00:51:13.801
Selvig?


00:51:13.966 --> 00:51:16.196
- He's an astrophysicist.
- He's a friend.


00:51:16.406 --> 00:51:18.442
Loki has him under some kind of spell,


00:51:18.606 --> 00:51:20.039
along with one of ours.


00:51:20.246 --> 00:51:21.759
I want to know why Loki let us take him.


00:51:21.886 --> 00:51:23.114
He's not leading an army from here.


00:51:23.326 --> 00:51:24.964
I don't think
we should be focusing on Loki.


00:51:25.166 --> 00:51:26.884
That guy's brain is a bag full of cats.


00:51:27.006 --> 00:51:28.234
You could smell crazy on him.


00:51:28.446 --> 00:51:30.118
Have care how you speak.


00:51:30.646 --> 00:51:32.762
Loki is beyond reason,
but he is of Asgard.


00:51:33.166 --> 00:51:34.201
And he is my brother.


00:51:34.406 --> 00:51:36.203
He killed 80 people in two days.


00:51:37.046 --> 00:51:38.001
He's adopted.


00:51:38.166 --> 00:51:40.361
I think it's about the mechanics.


00:51:40.566 --> 00:51:42.443
Iridium... What do they
need the iridium for?


00:51:42.646 --> 00:51:43.602
It's a stabilising agent.


00:51:43.767 --> 00:51:44.995
I'm just saying, pick a weekend.


00:51:45.127 --> 00:51:46.606
I'll fly you to Portland.


00:51:46.807 --> 00:51:48.286
Keep love alive.


00:51:48.487 --> 00:51:50.284
It means the portal
won't collapse on itself


00:51:50.447 --> 00:51:52.199
like it did at S.H.I.E.L.D.


00:51:52.407 --> 00:51:55.558
No hard feelings, Point Break.
You've got a mean swing.


00:51:55.767 --> 00:51:57.917
Also, it means the portal
can open as wide


00:51:58.127 --> 00:52:00.436
and stay open as long, as Loki wants.


00:52:01.127 --> 00:52:03.243
Raise the mizzenmast. Jib the topsails.


00:52:04.887 --> 00:52:06.036
<i>That man is playing Galaga.</i>


00:52:07.047 --> 00:52:10.278
He thought we wouldn't notice,
but we did.


00:52:12.167 --> 00:52:13.486
How does Fury even see these?


00:52:13.647 --> 00:52:14.602
He turns.


00:52:14.887 --> 00:52:16.445
Sounds exhausting.


00:52:17.487 --> 00:52:18.602
The rest of the raw materials,


00:52:18.807 --> 00:52:21.480
Agent Barton can get
his hands on pretty easily.


00:52:21.687 --> 00:52:23.006
The only major component
he still needs


00:52:23.207 --> 00:52:26.563
is a power source
of high-energy density.


00:52:26.767 --> 00:52:29.884
Something to kick-start the Cube.


00:52:30.087 --> 00:52:32.921
When did you become an expert
in thermonuclear astrophysics?


00:52:33.128 --> 00:52:34.083
Last night.


00:52:34.568 --> 00:52:37.640
The packet, Selvig's notes,
the extraction theory papers.


00:52:37.848 --> 00:52:38.803
Am I the only one who did the reading?


00:52:38.968 --> 00:52:41.641
Does Loki need any particular
kind of power source?


00:52:41.848 --> 00:52:44.442
He would have to heat the Cube
to 120-million Kelvin


00:52:44.648 --> 00:52:46.047
just to break through
the Coulomb barrier.


00:52:46.248 --> 00:52:48.364
Unless Selvig has figured out
how to stabilise


00:52:48.568 --> 00:52:49.637
the quantum tunnelling effect.


00:52:49.848 --> 00:52:50.803
Well, if he could do that,


00:52:50.968 --> 00:52:53.323
he could achieve heavy ion fusion
at any reactor on the planet.


00:52:53.528 --> 00:52:55.837
Finally, someone who speaks English.


00:52:56.048 --> 00:52:57.925
Is that what just happened?


00:52:58.128 --> 00:53:00.039
It's good to meet you, Dr Banner.


00:53:00.248 --> 00:53:03.160
Your work on antielectron
collisions is unparalleled.


00:53:03.368 --> 00:53:05.086
And I'm a huge fan of the way
you lose control


00:53:05.288 --> 00:53:07.244
and turn into an enormous
green rage-monster.


00:53:08.728 --> 00:53:09.717
Thanks.


00:53:09.928 --> 00:53:12.317
Dr Banner is only here
to track the Cube.


00:53:12.528 --> 00:53:13.756
I was hoping you might join him.


00:53:13.968 --> 00:53:15.083
I would start with that stick of his.


00:53:15.208 --> 00:53:16.197
It may be magical,


00:53:16.328 --> 00:53:17.556
but it works an awful lot
like a HYDRA weapon.


00:53:17.688 --> 00:53:20.601
I don't know about that,
but it is powered by the Cube.


00:53:20.889 --> 00:53:22.561
And I would like to know
how Loki used it


00:53:22.769 --> 00:53:24.282
to turn two of the sharpest men I know


00:53:24.409 --> 00:53:26.127
into his personal flying monkeys.


00:53:26.489 --> 00:53:27.968
Monkeys? I do not understand.


00:53:28.089 --> 00:53:29.044
I do.


00:53:31.929 --> 00:53:33.726
I understood that reference.


00:53:34.609 --> 00:53:35.883
Shall we play, Doctor?


00:53:36.089 --> 00:53:37.727
This way, sir.


00:53:51.129 --> 00:53:52.642
The gamma readings
are definitely consistent


00:53:52.849 --> 00:53:54.760
with Selvig's reports of the Tesseract.


00:53:55.129 --> 00:53:56.687
But it's going to take weeks to process.


00:53:56.889 --> 00:53:58.038
If we bypass their mainframe


00:53:58.169 --> 00:53:59.397
and direct route to the Homer cluster,


00:53:59.609 --> 00:54:02.567
we can clock this
at around 600 teraflops.


00:54:03.689 --> 00:54:05.566
All I packed was a toothbrush.


00:54:06.610 --> 00:54:08.123
You know, you should come by
Stark Tower sometime.


00:54:08.330 --> 00:54:10.286
Top ten floors, all R&D.


00:54:10.610 --> 00:54:12.009
You'd love it. It's Candy Land.


00:54:12.210 --> 00:54:14.599
Thanks, but the last time
I was in New York,


00:54:14.810 --> 00:54:17.244
I kind of broke Harlem.


00:54:17.450 --> 00:54:19.202
Well, I promise
a stress-free environment.


00:54:19.410 --> 00:54:21.128
No tension, no surprises.


00:54:22.570 --> 00:54:24.003
- Hey!
- Nothing?


00:54:24.210 --> 00:54:25.165
Are you nuts?


00:54:25.290 --> 00:54:26.245
Jury's out.


00:54:26.370 --> 00:54:27.439
You really have got
a lid on it, haven't you?


00:54:27.570 --> 00:54:28.525
What's your secret?


00:54:28.650 --> 00:54:30.049
Mellow jazz, bongo drums,
huge bag of weed?


00:54:30.210 --> 00:54:31.279
Is everything a joke to you?


00:54:31.570 --> 00:54:32.525
Funny things are.


00:54:32.650 --> 00:54:34.322
Threatening the safety
of everyone on this ship


00:54:34.450 --> 00:54:35.644
isn't funny.


00:54:35.770 --> 00:54:36.725
No offence, Doc.


00:54:36.850 --> 00:54:38.283
It's all right,
I wouldn't have come aboard


00:54:38.410 --> 00:54:41.129
if I couldn't handle pointy things.


00:54:41.250 --> 00:54:43.718
You're tip-toeing, big man.
You need to strut.


00:54:43.850 --> 00:54:45.442
And you need to focus
on the problem, Mr Stark.


00:54:45.570 --> 00:54:47.003
Do you think I'm not?


00:54:47.130 --> 00:54:49.803
Why did Fury call us in?
Why now? Why not before?


00:54:49.930 --> 00:54:51.602
What isn't he telling us?


00:54:51.730 --> 00:54:53.402
I can't do the equation unless
I have all the variables.


00:54:54.011 --> 00:54:55.205
You think Fury's hiding something?


00:54:55.331 --> 00:54:58.368
He's a spy. Captain, he's "the" spy.


00:54:58.491 --> 00:55:00.163
His secrets have secrets.


00:55:00.291 --> 00:55:01.724
It's bugging him, too. Isn't it?


00:55:04.211 --> 00:55:05.929
I just want to finish my work here, and...


00:55:06.051 --> 00:55:07.006
Doctor?


00:55:12.211 --> 00:55:14.486
"A warm light for all mankind."


00:55:14.611 --> 00:55:16.602
Loki's jab at Fury about the Cube.


00:55:16.731 --> 00:55:18.130
I heard it.


00:55:18.251 --> 00:55:20.446
I think that was meant for you.


00:55:21.131 --> 00:55:23.964
Even if Barton didn't
tell Loki about the tower,


00:55:24.091 --> 00:55:25.126
it was still all over the news.


00:55:25.251 --> 00:55:27.242
The Stark Tower? That big, ugly


00:55:28.531 --> 00:55:29.725
building in New York?


00:55:29.851 --> 00:55:33.400
It's powered by an arc reactor,
a self-sustaining energy source.


00:55:33.531 --> 00:55:35.840
That building will run itself
for, what, a year?


00:55:35.971 --> 00:55:37.723
It's just the prototype.


00:55:37.851 --> 00:55:39.728
I'm kind of the only name
in clean energy right now.


00:55:40.131 --> 00:55:41.484
That's what he's getting at.


00:55:41.611 --> 00:55:44.080
So, why didn't S.H.I.E.L.D. Bring him in
on the Tesseract project?


00:55:44.212 --> 00:55:45.884
What are they doing
in the energy business


00:55:46.012 --> 00:55:47.286
in the first place?


00:55:47.412 --> 00:55:50.245
I should probably look into that
once my decryption programme


00:55:50.372 --> 00:55:52.442
finishes breaking into all of
S.H.I.E.L.D.'s secure files.


00:55:52.572 --> 00:55:53.527
I'm sorry. Did you say...


00:55:53.652 --> 00:55:55.563
Jarvis has been running it
since I hit the bridge.


00:55:55.692 --> 00:55:57.205
In a few hours,
I'll know every dirty secret


00:55:57.332 --> 00:55:58.447
S.H.I.E.L.D. Has ever tried to hide.


00:55:58.572 --> 00:55:59.527
Blueberry?


00:55:59.652 --> 00:56:01.449
Yet you're confused about why
they didn't want you around.


00:56:01.572 --> 00:56:04.291
An intelligence organisation
that fears intelligence?


00:56:04.412 --> 00:56:05.925
Historically, not awesome.


00:56:06.052 --> 00:56:08.247
I think Loki's trying to wind us up.


00:56:08.372 --> 00:56:09.885
This is a man who means to start a war


00:56:10.012 --> 00:56:11.491
and if we don't stay focused,
he'll succeed.


00:56:12.732 --> 00:56:15.087
We have orders.
We should follow them.


00:56:15.572 --> 00:56:17.483
Following's not really my style.


00:56:18.652 --> 00:56:20.927
And you're all about style, aren't you?


00:56:21.052 --> 00:56:22.041
Of the people in this room,


00:56:22.172 --> 00:56:23.685
which one is,
A, wearing a spangly outfit,


00:56:23.812 --> 00:56:25.086
and, B, not of use?


00:56:25.212 --> 00:56:29.365
Steve, tell me none of this
smells a little funky to you.


00:56:31.973 --> 00:56:32.962
Just find the Cube.


00:56:45.373 --> 00:56:47.204
That's the guy
my dad never shut up about?


00:56:47.653 --> 00:56:50.326
I'm wondering if they shouldn't have
kept him on ice.


00:56:51.133 --> 00:56:52.771
The guy's not wrong about Loki.


00:56:52.893 --> 00:56:54.565
He does have the jump on us.


00:56:54.693 --> 00:56:57.287
What he's got is an Acme dynamite kit.


00:56:57.413 --> 00:56:59.165
It's going to blow up in his face.


00:56:59.293 --> 00:57:01.488
And I'm going to be there when it does.


00:57:01.773 --> 00:57:03.843
Yeah. I'll read all about it.


00:57:05.893 --> 00:57:07.121
Or you'll be suiting up
with the rest of us.


00:57:08.653 --> 00:57:12.089
You see, I don't get a suit of armour.


00:57:12.213 --> 00:57:15.410
I'm exposed. Like a nerve.


00:57:15.533 --> 00:57:17.206
It's a nightmare.


00:57:17.334 --> 00:57:20.007
I've got a cluster of shrapnel
trying every second


00:57:20.134 --> 00:57:22.045
to crawl its way into my heart.


00:57:22.174 --> 00:57:24.130
This stops it.


00:57:24.254 --> 00:57:26.484
This little circle of light,
it's part of me now,


00:57:27.654 --> 00:57:29.246
not just armour.


00:57:29.894 --> 00:57:32.249
It's a terrible privilege.


00:57:32.574 --> 00:57:34.849
- But you can control it.
- Because I learned how.


00:57:34.974 --> 00:57:35.929
It's different.


00:57:36.254 --> 00:57:39.451
Hey, I read all about your accident.


00:57:39.574 --> 00:57:42.771
That much gamma exposure
should have killed you.


00:57:42.894 --> 00:57:45.249
So you're saying that the Hulk...


00:57:46.654 --> 00:57:48.929
The other guy saved my life?


00:57:49.414 --> 00:57:50.483
That's nice.


00:57:51.334 --> 00:57:54.963
It's a nice sentiment. Saved it for what?


00:57:56.214 --> 00:57:58.045
I guess we'll find out.


00:57:59.694 --> 00:58:01.286
You may not enjoy that.


00:58:01.414 --> 00:58:03.291
And you just might.


00:59:00.096 --> 00:59:01.415
<i>As soon as Loki took the doctor,</i>


00:59:01.536 --> 00:59:03.208
we moved Jane Foster.


00:59:03.336 --> 00:59:05.611
They've got an excellent
observatory in Tromsø.


00:59:05.736 --> 00:59:09.126
She was asked to consult there
very suddenly yesterday.


00:59:09.256 --> 00:59:12.885
Handsome fee, private plane,
very remote.


00:59:13.736 --> 00:59:14.725
She'll be safe.


00:59:14.856 --> 00:59:16.175
Thank you.


00:59:17.896 --> 00:59:19.852
It's no accident, Loki taking Erik Selvig.


00:59:20.816 --> 00:59:23.284
I dread what he plans for him
once he's done.


00:59:23.416 --> 00:59:24.485
Erik is a good man.


00:59:24.616 --> 00:59:25.571
He talks about you a lot.


00:59:27.376 --> 00:59:29.287
You changed his life.


00:59:30.936 --> 00:59:32.733
You changed everything around here.


00:59:32.856 --> 00:59:34.892
They were better as they were.


00:59:35.456 --> 00:59:37.447
We pretend on Asgard
that we're more advanced


00:59:37.576 --> 00:59:41.126
but we come here,
battling like bilge snipe.


00:59:41.257 --> 00:59:43.009
- Like what?
- Bilge snipe.


00:59:43.137 --> 00:59:46.049
You know, huge, scaly, big antlers.


00:59:46.817 --> 00:59:48.535
- You don't have those?
- I don't think so.


00:59:48.657 --> 00:59:50.454
Well, they are repulsive.


00:59:51.737 --> 00:59:53.887
And they trample everything
in their path.


01:00:01.257 --> 01:00:04.454
When I first came to Earth,
Loki's rage followed me here,


01:00:04.577 --> 01:00:06.807
and your people paid the price.


01:00:06.937 --> 01:00:08.655
And now, again.


01:00:11.097 --> 01:00:13.452
In my youth, I courted war.


01:00:15.137 --> 01:00:17.048
War hasn't started yet.


01:00:18.137 --> 01:00:19.855
You think you could make Loki tell us


01:00:19.977 --> 01:00:21.205
where the Tesseract is?


01:00:21.337 --> 01:00:24.454
I do not know. Loki's mind is far afield.


01:00:24.577 --> 01:00:29.094
It's not just power he craves,
it's vengeance, upon me.


01:00:29.218 --> 01:00:31.254
There's no pain
would prise his need from him.


01:00:32.298 --> 01:00:34.414
A lot of guys think that


01:00:34.538 --> 01:00:35.971
until the pain starts.


01:00:38.178 --> 01:00:39.611
What are you asking me to do?


01:00:39.738 --> 01:00:43.174
I'm asking,
what are you prepared to do?


01:00:43.298 --> 01:00:44.287
Loki is a prisoner.


01:00:44.418 --> 01:00:46.648
Then why do I feel like
he's the only person on this boat


01:00:46.778 --> 01:00:48.291
that wants to be here?


01:01:00.378 --> 01:01:03.336
There's not many people
who can sneak up on me.


01:01:03.458 --> 01:01:05.050
But you figured I'd come.


01:01:05.698 --> 01:01:07.211
After.


01:01:08.058 --> 01:01:11.334
After whatever tortures
Fury can concoct,


01:01:11.458 --> 01:01:14.973
you would appear
as a friend, as a balm.


01:01:15.899 --> 01:01:17.491
And I would cooperate.


01:01:17.619 --> 01:01:19.530
I want to know what
you've done to Agent Barton.


01:01:19.659 --> 01:01:21.570
I would say I've expanded his mind.


01:01:24.059 --> 01:01:25.890
And once you've won,


01:01:26.739 --> 01:01:27.967
once you're king of the mountain,


01:01:30.019 --> 01:01:32.408
what happens to his mind?


01:01:33.619 --> 01:01:35.337
Is this love, Agent Romanoff?


01:01:35.459 --> 01:01:38.178
Love is for children. I owe him a debt.


01:01:41.899 --> 01:01:43.696
Tell me.


01:01:47.859 --> 01:01:50.976
Before I worked for S.H.I.E.L. D... I...


01:01:53.299 --> 01:01:57.053
Well, I made a name for myself.


01:01:57.179 --> 01:02:00.057
I have a very specific skill set.


01:02:00.179 --> 01:02:03.695
I didn't care who I used it for, or on.


01:02:04.660 --> 01:02:08.016
I got on S.H.I.E.L.D.'s radar
in a bad way.


01:02:09.140 --> 01:02:11.938
Agent Barton was sent to kill me.


01:02:12.940 --> 01:02:14.419
He made a different call.


01:02:16.300 --> 01:02:19.212
And what will you do
if I vow to spare him?


01:02:19.580 --> 01:02:20.854
Not let you out.


01:02:20.980 --> 01:02:22.777
No, but I like this.


01:02:23.660 --> 01:02:26.936
Your world in the balance,
and you bargain for one man.


01:02:27.060 --> 01:02:29.051
Regimes fall every day.


01:02:29.180 --> 01:02:31.614
I tend not to weep over that.
I'm Russian.


01:02:31.740 --> 01:02:32.695
Or I was.


01:02:33.940 --> 01:02:35.532
And what are you now?


01:02:35.980 --> 01:02:38.813
It's really not that complicated.


01:02:38.940 --> 01:02:42.853
I got red in my ledger,
I'd like to wipe it out.


01:02:43.820 --> 01:02:45.299
Can you?


01:02:46.580 --> 01:02:50.209
Can you wipe out that much red?


01:02:51.341 --> 01:02:53.059
Dreykov's daughter,


01:02:54.421 --> 01:02:56.173
São Paulo,


01:02:57.181 --> 01:02:59.570
the hospital fire?


01:03:00.381 --> 01:03:02.656
Barton told me everything.


01:03:02.781 --> 01:03:05.739
Your ledger is dripping. It's gushing red


01:03:05.861 --> 01:03:08.250
and you think saving a man
no more virtuous than yourself


01:03:08.381 --> 01:03:09.700
will change anything?


01:03:09.821 --> 01:03:12.381
This is the basest sentimentality.


01:03:12.501 --> 01:03:14.651
This is a child at prayer.


01:03:14.781 --> 01:03:16.009
Pathetic!


01:03:16.781 --> 01:03:19.249
<i>You lie and kill</i>


01:03:19.381 --> 01:03:22.293
<i>in the service of liars and killers.</i>


01:03:25.261 --> 01:03:28.298
<i>You pretend to be separate,
to have your own code,</i>


01:03:28.421 --> 01:03:31.015
<i>something that makes up
for the horrors.</i>


01:03:32.141 --> 01:03:34.450
<i>But they are part of you.</i>


01:03:34.581 --> 01:03:38.211
<i>And they will never go away.</i>


01:03:38.782 --> 01:03:42.138
I won't touch Barton,
not until I make him kill you.


01:03:42.262 --> 01:03:44.412
Slowly, intimately,


01:03:44.542 --> 01:03:46.817
in every way he knows you fear.


01:03:46.942 --> 01:03:49.900
And then he'll wake just long
enough to see his good work


01:03:50.022 --> 01:03:53.332
and when he screams, I'll split his skull.


01:03:53.462 --> 01:03:56.454
This is my bargain, you mewling quim.


01:03:57.982 --> 01:03:59.495
You're a monster.


01:04:01.622 --> 01:04:03.055
Oh, no.


01:04:03.902 --> 01:04:05.415
You brought the monster.


01:04:08.302 --> 01:04:09.815
So, Banner.


01:04:10.822 --> 01:04:11.937
That's your play.


01:04:12.062 --> 01:04:13.051
What?


01:04:13.982 --> 01:04:15.574
Loki means to unleash the Hulk.


01:04:15.702 --> 01:04:17.101
Keep Banner in the lab. I'm on my way.


01:04:17.222 --> 01:04:18.257
Send Thor as well.


01:04:19.862 --> 01:04:21.136
Thank you


01:04:21.262 --> 01:04:23.332
for your cooperation.


01:04:30.543 --> 01:04:31.942
What are you doing, Mr Stark?


01:04:32.063 --> 01:04:34.452
Kind of been wondering
the same thing about you.


01:04:34.583 --> 01:04:36.380
You're supposed to be locating
the Tesseract.


01:04:36.503 --> 01:04:38.016
We are. The model's locked


01:04:38.143 --> 01:04:39.371
and we're sweeping
for the signature now.


01:04:39.503 --> 01:04:40.458
When we get a hit,


01:04:40.583 --> 01:04:42.460
we'll have the location
within half a mile.


01:04:42.583 --> 01:04:44.983
Yeah, then you get your
Cube back. No muss, no fuss.


01:04:44.983 --> 01:04:46.655
Yeah, then you get your
Cube back. No muss, no fuss.


01:04:46.783 --> 01:04:47.852
What is "Phase 2"?


01:04:49.983 --> 01:04:52.702
Phase 2 is S.H.I.E.L.D. Uses
the Cube to make weapons.


01:04:52.823 --> 01:04:54.495
Sorry, computer was moving
a little slow for me.


01:04:54.623 --> 01:04:57.217
Rogers, we gathered everything
related to the Tesseract.


01:04:57.343 --> 01:04:58.742
This does not mean that we're making...


01:04:58.863 --> 01:04:59.818
I'm sorry, Nick.


01:04:59.943 --> 01:05:02.138
What were you lying?


01:05:02.263 --> 01:05:03.457
I was wrong, Director.


01:05:03.583 --> 01:05:04.572
The world hasn't changed a bit.


01:05:04.703 --> 01:05:05.692
Did you know about this?


01:05:05.823 --> 01:05:07.097
You want to think about
removing yourself


01:05:07.223 --> 01:05:08.497
from this environment, Doctor?


01:05:08.623 --> 01:05:10.693
I was in Calcutta.
I was pretty well removed.


01:05:10.823 --> 01:05:11.938
Loki is manipulating you.


01:05:12.063 --> 01:05:13.577
And you've been doing what, exactly?


01:05:13.704 --> 01:05:15.296
You didn't come here because
I bat my eyelashes at you.


01:05:15.424 --> 01:05:16.493
Yes, and I'm not leaving


01:05:16.624 --> 01:05:17.852
because suddenly
you get a little twitchy.


01:05:17.984 --> 01:05:19.542
I'd like to know why S.H.I.E.L.D.


01:05:19.664 --> 01:05:23.213
Is using the Tesseract
to build weapons of mass destruction.


01:05:23.824 --> 01:05:24.893
Because of him.


01:05:26.144 --> 01:05:27.099
Me?


01:05:28.024 --> 01:05:30.299
Last year, Earth had a visitor
from another planet


01:05:30.424 --> 01:05:33.461
who had a grudge match
that levelled a small town.


01:05:33.584 --> 01:05:35.700
We learned that
not only are we not alone


01:05:35.824 --> 01:05:39.260
but we are hopelessly,
hilariously, outgunned.


01:05:39.384 --> 01:05:41.534
My people want nothing
but peace with your planet.


01:05:41.664 --> 01:05:43.541
But you're not the only people
out there, are you?


01:05:43.664 --> 01:05:45.541
And you're not the only threat.


01:05:45.664 --> 01:05:48.701
The world's filling up with
people who can't be matched,


01:05:49.344 --> 01:05:50.493
that can't be controlled.


01:05:50.624 --> 01:05:51.693
Like you controlled the Cube?


01:05:51.824 --> 01:05:53.018
Your work with the Tesseract


01:05:53.144 --> 01:05:55.612
is what drew Loki to it, and his allies.


01:05:55.744 --> 01:05:57.063
It is a signal to all the realms


01:05:57.184 --> 01:05:59.744
that the Earth is ready
for a higher form of war.


01:05:59.864 --> 01:06:00.900
A higher form?


01:06:01.025 --> 01:06:01.980
You forced our hand.


01:06:02.105 --> 01:06:03.060
We had to come up with something.


01:06:03.185 --> 01:06:04.140
A nuclear deterrent.


01:06:04.265 --> 01:06:06.176
Because that always
calms everything right down.


01:06:06.305 --> 01:06:08.580
Remind me again how
you made your fortune, Stark.


01:06:08.705 --> 01:06:10.980
I'm sure if he still made weapons,
Stark would be neck-deep...


01:06:11.105 --> 01:06:12.663
Hold on. How is this now about me?


01:06:12.785 --> 01:06:13.854
I'm sorry, isn't everything?


01:06:13.985 --> 01:06:15.782
I thought humans were
more evolved than this.


01:06:15.905 --> 01:06:18.658
Excuse me, did we come to
your planet and blow stuff up?


01:06:18.785 --> 01:06:20.582
You treat your champions
with such mistrust.


01:06:20.705 --> 01:06:22.104
Are you boys really that naïve?


01:06:22.225 --> 01:06:24.022
S.H.I.E.L.D. Monitors potential threats.


01:06:24.145 --> 01:06:25.373
Captain America's on threat watch?


01:06:25.505 --> 01:06:26.460
We all are.


01:06:26.585 --> 01:06:27.938
Wait, you're on that list?


01:06:28.065 --> 01:06:29.544
Are you above or below angry bees?


01:06:29.665 --> 01:06:31.701
Stark, so help me God,
if you make one more wisecrack...


01:06:31.825 --> 01:06:33.019
Threat! Verbal threat. I feel threatened.


01:06:33.145 --> 01:06:35.534
- Show some respect.
- Respect what?


01:06:42.585 --> 01:06:45.383
<i>Transport Six-Six-Bravo,
please relay confirm codes.</i>


01:06:45.505 --> 01:06:47.575
<i>I've got you on the computer,
but not on the day log.</i>


01:06:47.705 --> 01:06:49.697
<i>What is your haul? Over.</i>


01:06:49.826 --> 01:06:52.340
<i>Arms and ammunition. Over.</i>


01:07:00.346 --> 01:07:02.462
You speak of control,
yet you court chaos.


01:07:02.586 --> 01:07:04.224
That's his M.O., isn't it?


01:07:04.346 --> 01:07:05.540
I mean, what are we, a team?


01:07:05.666 --> 01:07:08.499
No, we're a chemical mixture
that makes chaos.


01:07:08.626 --> 01:07:10.503
We're a time bomb.


01:07:10.626 --> 01:07:12.378
You need to step away.


01:07:12.506 --> 01:07:14.258
Why shouldn't the guy
let off a little steam?


01:07:14.386 --> 01:07:16.422
You know damn well why. Back off!


01:07:16.546 --> 01:07:18.662
I'm starting to want you to make me.


01:07:18.786 --> 01:07:22.256
Yeah. Big man in a suit of armour.


01:07:22.386 --> 01:07:23.785
Take that off, what are you?


01:07:23.906 --> 01:07:26.136
Genius, billionaire,
playboy, philanthropist.


01:07:26.986 --> 01:07:30.023
I know guys with none of that
worth ten of you.


01:07:30.146 --> 01:07:31.101
I've seen the footage.


01:07:31.226 --> 01:07:33.376
The only thing you really
fight for is yourself.


01:07:34.786 --> 01:07:36.618
You're not the guy
to make the sacrifice play,


01:07:36.747 --> 01:07:39.136
to lay down on a wire and let
the other guy crawl over you.


01:07:39.267 --> 01:07:41.303
I think I would just cut the wire.


01:07:43.827 --> 01:07:45.943
Always a way out.


01:07:46.067 --> 01:07:47.261
You may not be a threat


01:07:47.387 --> 01:07:49.218
but you better stop pretending
to be a hero.


01:07:49.347 --> 01:07:51.702
A hero? Like you?


01:07:51.827 --> 01:07:53.783
You're a laboratory experiment, Rogers.


01:07:53.907 --> 01:07:57.377
Everything special about you
came out of a bottle.


01:08:21.627 --> 01:08:24.347
Put on the suit. Let's go a few rounds.


01:08:25.308 --> 01:08:28.618
You people are so petty and tiny.


01:08:28.748 --> 01:08:29.703
Yeah, this is a team.


01:08:29.828 --> 01:08:31.022
Agent Romanoff, would you escort


01:08:31.148 --> 01:08:32.217
Dr Banner back to his...


01:08:32.348 --> 01:08:33.940
Where? You rented my room.


01:08:34.068 --> 01:08:35.467
The cell was just in case...


01:08:35.588 --> 01:08:37.067
In case you needed to kill me.


01:08:37.188 --> 01:08:39.986
But you can't. I know, I tried.


01:08:42.588 --> 01:08:45.386
I got low. I didn't see an end.


01:08:45.508 --> 01:08:49.786
So, I put a bullet in my mouth,
and the other guy spit it out.


01:08:50.348 --> 01:08:51.497
So I moved on.


01:08:51.628 --> 01:08:54.347
I focused on helping
other people. I was good.


01:08:54.468 --> 01:08:56.584
Until you dragged me back
into this freak show


01:08:56.708 --> 01:08:58.027
and put everyone here at risk.


01:08:58.148 --> 01:09:00.139
You want to know my secret,
Agent Romanoff?


01:09:00.268 --> 01:09:02.020
You want to know how I stay calm?


01:09:04.708 --> 01:09:06.778
Dr Banner,


01:09:07.548 --> 01:09:08.822
put down the sceptre.


01:09:17.229 --> 01:09:18.344
Got it.


01:09:19.149 --> 01:09:20.104
Sorry, kids,


01:09:20.229 --> 01:09:21.901
you don't get to see
my party trick after all.


01:09:22.029 --> 01:09:22.984
You located the Tesseract?


01:09:23.109 --> 01:09:24.064
I could get there fastest.


01:09:24.189 --> 01:09:26.225
The Tesseract belongs on Asgard.
No human is a match for it.


01:09:26.349 --> 01:09:27.623
- You're not going alone.
- You're gonna stop me?


01:09:27.749 --> 01:09:28.704
Put on the suit, let's find out.


01:09:28.829 --> 01:09:30.057
I'm not afraid to hit an old man.


01:09:30.189 --> 01:09:31.144
Put on the suit.


01:09:33.909 --> 01:09:35.467
Oh, my God.


01:09:50.349 --> 01:09:51.304
Put on the suit.


01:09:51.429 --> 01:09:52.657
Yeah.


01:09:55.309 --> 01:09:56.981
<i>All hands to stations.</i>


01:10:00.950 --> 01:10:02.668
<i>- Hill!
- External detonation.</i>


01:10:02.790 --> 01:10:03.984
Number three engine is down.


01:10:04.110 --> 01:10:05.065
We've been hit.


01:10:05.190 --> 01:10:06.305
- Can they get it running?
- Fire in engine three!


01:10:06.430 --> 01:10:07.385
Talk to me.


01:10:07.510 --> 01:10:09.068
Turbine looks mostly intact


01:10:09.190 --> 01:10:10.987
but it's impossible to
get out there to make repairs


01:10:11.110 --> 01:10:12.463
while we're in the air.


01:10:12.590 --> 01:10:15.024
If we lose one more engine,
we won't be.


01:10:15.150 --> 01:10:17.061
Somebody's got to get outside
and patch that engine.


01:10:17.190 --> 01:10:18.828
<i>- Stark, you copy that?
- I'm on it.</i>


01:10:18.950 --> 01:10:22.101
<i>Coulson, initiate defensive lockdown
in the detention section</i>


01:10:22.230 --> 01:10:23.185
<i>then get to the armoury.</i>


01:10:23.310 --> 01:10:24.379
Romanoff?


01:10:27.870 --> 01:10:29.269
We're okay.


01:10:31.750 --> 01:10:32.944
We're okay, right?


01:10:45.030 --> 01:10:46.179
- Keep that engine down!
- Yes, sir.


01:10:46.310 --> 01:10:47.949
Detention, wait for cameras to go dark.


01:10:48.071 --> 01:10:49.789
- Got it.
- Stay close.


01:10:51.471 --> 01:10:52.904
Let's go, Level 4.


01:10:53.831 --> 01:10:56.504
Engine three. I'll meet you there.


01:11:04.351 --> 01:11:05.466
Doctor?


01:11:07.751 --> 01:11:08.706
Bruce?


01:11:08.991 --> 01:11:12.506
You got to fight it.
This is just what Loki wants.


01:11:13.831 --> 01:11:14.820
We're going to be okay. Listen to me.


01:11:14.951 --> 01:11:15.906
Are you hurt?


01:11:19.071 --> 01:11:21.187
We're going to be okay. All right?


01:11:21.311 --> 01:11:23.950
I swear on my life,
I will get you out of this.


01:11:24.071 --> 01:11:25.390
You will walk away and never ever...


01:11:25.511 --> 01:11:27.502
Your life?


01:11:43.352 --> 01:11:44.307
Bruce.


01:12:19.672 --> 01:12:20.312
Bring the carrier about
to a 1-8-0, heading south!


01:12:20.312 --> 01:12:22.702
Bring the carrier about
to a 1-8-0, heading south!


01:12:22.833 --> 01:12:24.630
- Take us to the water!
- We're flying blind.


01:12:24.753 --> 01:12:26.664
Navigation's recalibrating
after the engine failure.


01:12:26.793 --> 01:12:28.465
Is the sun coming up?


01:12:29.193 --> 01:12:31.309
- Yes, sir.
- Then put it on the left.


01:12:31.433 --> 01:12:33.025
Get us over water.


01:12:33.153 --> 01:12:35.144
One more turbine goes down,
and we drop.


01:12:37.313 --> 01:12:38.541
Thanks.


01:12:41.753 --> 01:12:42.868
Stark!


01:12:45.473 --> 01:12:47.065
Stark, I'm here!


01:12:47.193 --> 01:12:48.626
<i>Good.</i>


01:12:49.793 --> 01:12:51.704
<i>Let's see what we've got.</i>


01:12:51.833 --> 01:12:53.425
I got to get this
superconducting coolant system


01:12:53.553 --> 01:12:54.508
back online


01:12:54.633 --> 01:12:56.032
before I can access the rotors,


01:12:56.153 --> 01:12:57.905
work on dislodging the debris.


01:13:00.353 --> 01:13:01.832
<i>I need you to get to that
engine control panel</i>


01:13:01.953 --> 01:13:05.468
<i>and tell me which relays
are in overload position.</i>


01:13:17.274 --> 01:13:18.753
<i>What does it look like in there?</i>


01:13:19.434 --> 01:13:21.868
It seems to run
on some form of electricity.


01:13:21.994 --> 01:13:23.666
Well, you're not wrong.


01:14:24.875 --> 01:14:27.594
We are not your enemies, Banner.


01:14:27.715 --> 01:14:28.670
Try to think!


01:14:38.395 --> 01:14:40.192
<i>Okay, the relays are intact.</i>


01:14:40.315 --> 01:14:41.714
What's our next move?


01:14:41.835 --> 01:14:42.790
<i>Even if I clear the rotors,</i>


01:14:42.915 --> 01:14:45.032
<i>this thing won't
re-engage without a jump.</i>


01:14:45.156 --> 01:14:46.475
I'm going to have to
get in there and push.


01:14:46.596 --> 01:14:48.268
If that thing gets up to
speed, you'll get shredded.


01:14:48.396 --> 01:14:50.307
That stator control unit
can reverse the polarity


01:14:50.436 --> 01:14:51.789
long enough to disengage
maglev and that could...


01:14:51.916 --> 01:14:53.190
Speak English!


01:14:54.476 --> 01:14:55.545
You see that red lever?


01:14:56.796 --> 01:14:58.832
<i>It will slow the rotors down
long enough for me to get out.</i>


01:14:58.956 --> 01:15:00.674
Stand by it. Wait for my word.


01:15:51.117 --> 01:15:52.835
We need full evac
on the lower hangar bay.


01:15:55.917 --> 01:15:56.906
Grenade!


01:16:11.437 --> 01:16:12.711
<i>We've got a perimeter breach!</i>


01:16:12.837 --> 01:16:14.793
<i>Hostiles are in S.H.I.E.L.D. Gear.</i>


01:16:14.917 --> 01:16:16.908
<i>Call-outs at every junction.</i>


01:16:23.918 --> 01:16:26.034
<i>We have the Hulk and Thor
on Research Level 4.</i>


01:16:26.158 --> 01:16:27.637
<i>Levels 2 and 3 are dark.</i>


01:16:27.758 --> 01:16:29.794
Sir, the Hulk will tear this place apart!


01:16:30.958 --> 01:16:31.913
Get his attention.


01:16:32.038 --> 01:16:36.031
Escort 6-0, proceed to
Wishbone and engage hostile.


01:16:36.158 --> 01:16:37.386
<i>Don't get too close.</i>


01:16:37.518 --> 01:16:38.837
<i>Copy.</i>


01:16:50.278 --> 01:16:51.597
<i>Target acquired.</i>


01:16:55.718 --> 01:16:56.673
<i>Target engaged.</i>


01:17:07.839 --> 01:17:09.318
<i>Target angry, target angry!</i>


01:18:14.920 --> 01:18:17.036
They're not getting through
here, so what the hell...


01:18:34.680 --> 01:18:36.830
<i>Engine one is now in shut-down.</i>


01:18:44.921 --> 01:18:46.991
We are in an uncontrolled descent.


01:18:47.121 --> 01:18:48.918
<i>Sir, we've lost all power in engine one.</i>


01:18:49.441 --> 01:18:51.193
<i>It's Barton. He took out our systems.</i>


01:18:51.321 --> 01:18:53.710
<i>He's headed for the detention level.</i>


01:18:53.841 --> 01:18:55.718
<i>Does anybody copy?</i>


01:18:56.841 --> 01:18:58.877
This is Agent Romanoff.


01:18:59.001 --> 01:19:00.400
I copy.


01:19:04.841 --> 01:19:05.796
<i>Stark, we're losing altitude.</i>


01:19:05.921 --> 01:19:07.320
Yeah, I noticed.


01:19:35.162 --> 01:19:36.151
No!


01:19:43.442 --> 01:19:46.036
Are you ever not going to fall for that?


01:20:27.283 --> 01:20:29.433
The humans think us immortal.


01:20:30.483 --> 01:20:31.962
Should we test that?


01:20:34.643 --> 01:20:35.792
Move away, please.


01:20:40.083 --> 01:20:41.516
You like this?


01:20:42.443 --> 01:20:45.560
We started working on the prototype
after you sent the Destroyer.


01:20:46.723 --> 01:20:48.873
Even I don't know what it does.


01:20:49.643 --> 01:20:50.837
Do you want to find out?


01:20:52.763 --> 01:20:54.162
No!


01:22:00.845 --> 01:22:02.198
Natasha?


01:22:32.485 --> 01:22:34.157
You're going to lose.


01:22:36.125 --> 01:22:37.274
Am I?


01:22:38.525 --> 01:22:40.914
It's in your nature.


01:22:43.006 --> 01:22:45.236
Your heroes are scattered.


01:22:45.366 --> 01:22:48.915
Your floating fortress falls from the sky.


01:22:49.046 --> 01:22:50.604
Where is my disadvantage?


01:22:51.246 --> 01:22:53.237
You lack conviction.


01:22:54.046 --> 01:22:55.001
I don't think I'm...


01:23:01.566 --> 01:23:03.206
So, that's what it does.


01:23:05.206 --> 01:23:08.198
<i>All hands
to crash stations immediately.</i>


01:23:34.687 --> 01:23:35.642
Cap, hit the lever.


01:23:36.007 --> 01:23:38.475
I need a minute here!


01:23:38.607 --> 01:23:39.642
Lever


01:23:39.767 --> 01:23:40.836
now!


01:23:52.327 --> 01:23:53.396
<i>Help!</i>


01:24:27.568 --> 01:24:28.887
Sorry, boss.


01:24:29.008 --> 01:24:30.646
The god rabbited.


01:24:30.768 --> 01:24:32.167
Just stay awake.


01:24:32.288 --> 01:24:33.846
Eyes on me.


01:24:33.968 --> 01:24:35.447
No, I'm clocking out here.


01:24:35.568 --> 01:24:37.001
Not an option.


01:24:37.968 --> 01:24:39.845
It's okay, boss.


01:24:41.688 --> 01:24:43.644
This was never gonna work


01:24:43.768 --> 01:24:44.996
if they didn't have something


01:24:46.288 --> 01:24:47.767
to...


01:25:15.689 --> 01:25:17.441
<i>Agent Coulson is down.</i>


01:25:18.769 --> 01:25:20.407
<i>A medical team is on
its way to your location.</i>


01:25:20.529 --> 01:25:21.928
<i>They're here.</i>


01:25:25.009 --> 01:25:26.567
<i>They called it.</i>


01:25:42.369 --> 01:25:43.927
These were in Phil Coulson's jacket.


01:25:47.129 --> 01:25:49.165
I guess he never did
get you to sign them.


01:25:52.530 --> 01:25:54.122
We're dead in the air up here.


01:25:54.250 --> 01:25:57.208
Our communications,
the location of the Cube,


01:25:57.330 --> 01:25:59.639
Banner, Thor...


01:26:00.890 --> 01:26:02.721
I got nothing for you.


01:26:02.850 --> 01:26:05.648
I lost my one good eye.


01:26:08.570 --> 01:26:11.448
Maybe I had that coming.


01:26:15.490 --> 01:26:16.718
Yes,


01:26:17.850 --> 01:26:21.047
we were going to build
an arsenal with the Tesseract.


01:26:22.450 --> 01:26:24.281
I never put all my chips
on that number, though


01:26:24.410 --> 01:26:27.322
because I was playing
something even riskier.


01:26:31.130 --> 01:26:35.089
There was an idea, Stark knows this,


01:26:36.890 --> 01:26:40.088
called the Avengers Initiative.


01:26:41.251 --> 01:26:43.287
The idea was to bring together a group


01:26:43.411 --> 01:26:45.845
of remarkable people


01:26:46.611 --> 01:26:49.330
to see if they could become
something more.


01:26:50.651 --> 01:26:54.644
To see if they could work together
when we needed them to,


01:26:54.771 --> 01:26:57.968
to fight the battles that we never could.


01:27:00.611 --> 01:27:05.241
Phil Coulson died
still believing in that idea.


01:27:07.491 --> 01:27:09.083
In heroes.


01:27:16.851 --> 01:27:18.330
Well,


01:27:19.171 --> 01:27:21.731
it's an old-fashioned notion.


01:27:41.212 --> 01:27:43.601
<i>You fell out of the sky.</i>


01:27:57.052 --> 01:27:58.485
Did I hurt anybody?


01:27:58.612 --> 01:28:01.524
There's nobody around here to get hurt.


01:28:01.652 --> 01:28:04.803
You did scare the hell
out of some pigeons, though.


01:28:05.612 --> 01:28:06.601
Lucky.


01:28:06.732 --> 01:28:08.290
Or just good aim.


01:28:08.412 --> 01:28:09.925
You were awake when you fell.


01:28:11.932 --> 01:28:13.888
- You saw?
- The whole thing.


01:28:14.012 --> 01:28:15.571
Right through the ceiling.


01:28:15.693 --> 01:28:19.481
Big and green and buck-ass nude.


01:28:19.613 --> 01:28:20.682
Here.


01:28:22.013 --> 01:28:24.083
Didn't think those would
fit you until you shrunk down


01:28:24.213 --> 01:28:26.522
to a regular-size feller.


01:28:28.773 --> 01:28:30.001
Thank you.


01:28:30.973 --> 01:28:32.167
Are you an alien?


01:28:32.733 --> 01:28:33.882
What?


01:28:34.173 --> 01:28:35.447
From outer space, an alien.


01:28:36.053 --> 01:28:37.008
No.


01:28:37.373 --> 01:28:40.365
Well, then, son, you've got a condition.


01:28:50.773 --> 01:28:53.003
Clint. You're going to be all right.


01:28:56.213 --> 01:28:58.204
You know that?


01:28:59.013 --> 01:29:00.810
Is that what you know?


01:29:03.174 --> 01:29:05.927
I've got no window.


01:29:06.694 --> 01:29:08.014
I have to flush him out.


01:29:08.894 --> 01:29:10.646
You got to level out.
It's going to take time.


01:29:10.774 --> 01:29:12.253
You don't understand.


01:29:14.134 --> 01:29:17.251
Have you ever had someone
take your brain and play?


01:29:18.014 --> 01:29:22.007
Pull you out
and stuff something else in?


01:29:25.054 --> 01:29:27.329
Do you know what it's like
to be unmade?


01:29:28.814 --> 01:29:31.089
You know that I do.


01:29:38.374 --> 01:29:39.363
Why am I back?


01:29:40.454 --> 01:29:41.773
How did you get him out?


01:29:41.894 --> 01:29:44.613
Cognitive recalibration.


01:29:44.734 --> 01:29:47.328
I hit you really hard on the head.


01:29:47.454 --> 01:29:48.489
Thanks.


01:29:52.615 --> 01:29:54.287
Natasha...


01:29:54.935 --> 01:29:55.970
How many agents did I...


01:29:56.095 --> 01:29:57.494
Don't.


01:29:57.615 --> 01:29:59.731
Don't do that to yourself, Clint.


01:30:00.295 --> 01:30:01.933
This is Loki.


01:30:02.055 --> 01:30:04.569
This is monsters and magic,


01:30:04.695 --> 01:30:06.253
and nothing we were ever trained for.


01:30:06.375 --> 01:30:07.854
Loki, did he get away?


01:30:07.975 --> 01:30:08.930
Yeah.


01:30:09.255 --> 01:30:11.405
I don't suppose you know where.


01:30:11.535 --> 01:30:13.253
I didn't need to know.


01:30:13.375 --> 01:30:15.047
I didn't ask.


01:30:18.175 --> 01:30:20.564
He's going to
make his play soon, though.


01:30:20.895 --> 01:30:21.850
Today.


01:30:21.975 --> 01:30:23.249
We got to stop him.


01:30:23.895 --> 01:30:25.089
Yeah? Who's "we"?


01:30:25.215 --> 01:30:27.092
I don't know. Whoever's left.


01:30:28.255 --> 01:30:29.529
Well,


01:30:31.175 --> 01:30:33.245
if I put an arrow
through Loki's eye socket,


01:30:33.375 --> 01:30:35.969
I would sleep better, I suppose.


01:30:38.696 --> 01:30:40.209
Now you sound like you.


01:30:40.896 --> 01:30:42.295
But you don't.


01:30:44.136 --> 01:30:46.855
You're a spy, not a soldier.


01:30:46.976 --> 01:30:51.527
Now you want to wade into a war. Why?


01:30:53.216 --> 01:30:55.093
What did Loki do to you?


01:30:55.816 --> 01:30:58.125
He didn't. I just...


01:31:01.736 --> 01:31:03.215
Natasha.


01:31:05.216 --> 01:31:07.127
I've been compromised.


01:31:10.096 --> 01:31:12.132
I got red in my ledger.


01:31:14.176 --> 01:31:16.167
I would like to wipe it out.


01:31:31.537 --> 01:31:32.970
Was he married?


01:31:33.097 --> 01:31:34.450
No.


01:31:34.577 --> 01:31:38.616
There was a cellist, I think.


01:31:40.137 --> 01:31:41.490
I'm sorry.


01:31:42.177 --> 01:31:43.769
He seemed like a good man.


01:31:45.017 --> 01:31:46.052
He was an idiot.


01:31:46.177 --> 01:31:48.327
Why? For believing?


01:31:48.457 --> 01:31:49.810
For taking on Loki alone.


01:31:49.937 --> 01:31:51.575
He was doing his job.


01:31:51.697 --> 01:31:54.131
He was out of his league.
He should have waited.


01:31:54.257 --> 01:31:55.246
He should have...


01:31:55.377 --> 01:31:56.890
Sometimes there isn't a way out, Tony.


01:31:57.017 --> 01:31:59.053
Right, I've heard that before.


01:31:59.177 --> 01:32:00.610
Is this the first time you lost a soldier?


01:32:00.737 --> 01:32:02.455
We are not soldiers.


01:32:06.737 --> 01:32:08.409
I'm not marching to Fury's fife.


01:32:08.537 --> 01:32:09.652
Neither am I.


01:32:09.777 --> 01:32:11.893
He's got the same blood
on his hands that Loki does.


01:32:12.017 --> 01:32:13.337
But right now,
we got to put that behind us


01:32:13.458 --> 01:32:15.574
and get this done.


01:32:15.698 --> 01:32:16.653
Loki needs a power source.


01:32:16.778 --> 01:32:17.733
If we can put together a list...


01:32:17.858 --> 01:32:18.813
He made it personal.


01:32:18.978 --> 01:32:19.967
That's not the point.


01:32:20.098 --> 01:32:22.373
That is the point. That's Loki's point.


01:32:22.498 --> 01:32:24.329
He hit us all right where we live. Why?


01:32:24.458 --> 01:32:25.413
To tear us apart.


01:32:25.538 --> 01:32:27.335
Yeah, divide and conquer is great


01:32:27.458 --> 01:32:29.813
but he knows he has to
take us out to win, right?


01:32:29.938 --> 01:32:31.417
That's what he wants.


01:32:31.538 --> 01:32:33.927
He wants to beat us,
he wants to be seen doing it.


01:32:34.058 --> 01:32:35.127
He wants an audience.


01:32:35.818 --> 01:32:37.410
Right. I caught his act in Stuttgart.


01:32:37.538 --> 01:32:40.336
Yeah, that was just previews.
This is opening night.


01:32:40.458 --> 01:32:42.892
And Loki, he's a full-tilt diva, right?


01:32:43.018 --> 01:32:44.531
He wants flowers, he wants parades.


01:32:44.658 --> 01:32:48.287
He wants a monument built to the skies
with his name plastered...


01:32:49.978 --> 01:32:51.491
Son of a bitch.


01:33:02.299 --> 01:33:03.288
Time to go.


01:33:03.419 --> 01:33:04.898
- Go where?
- I'll tell you on the way.


01:33:05.019 --> 01:33:05.974
Can you fly one of those jets?


01:33:07.499 --> 01:33:08.693
I can.


01:33:12.419 --> 01:33:13.408
You got a suit?


01:33:13.539 --> 01:33:14.494
Yeah.


01:33:14.619 --> 01:33:16.018
Then suit up.


01:33:42.539 --> 01:33:43.767
Hey, you guys aren't
authorised to be in here.


01:33:43.899 --> 01:33:46.129
Son, just don't.


01:33:48.100 --> 01:33:49.055
Sir.


01:33:49.180 --> 01:33:50.329
Agent Hill.


01:33:50.860 --> 01:33:52.339
Those cards,


01:33:54.380 --> 01:33:58.658
they were in Coulson's locker,
not in his jacket.


01:34:02.900 --> 01:34:04.413
They needed the push.


01:34:07.380 --> 01:34:09.575
<i>We have an unauthorised departure
from Bay 6.</i>


01:34:10.420 --> 01:34:11.694
They found him.


01:34:12.500 --> 01:34:16.049
Get our communications back up,
whatever you have to do.


01:34:16.180 --> 01:34:18.330
- I want eyes on everything.
- Yes, sir.


01:34:31.340 --> 01:34:33.012
<i>Sir, I've turned off the arc reactor</i>


01:34:33.140 --> 01:34:36.816
<i>but the device
is already self-sustaining.</i>


01:34:36.941 --> 01:34:39.011
<i>Shut it down, Dr Selvig.</i>


01:34:39.661 --> 01:34:40.889
It's too late!


01:34:42.861 --> 01:34:44.260
She can't stop now.


01:34:45.261 --> 01:34:47.616
She wants to show us something!


01:34:47.741 --> 01:34:49.697
A new universe.


01:34:49.821 --> 01:34:51.300
<i>Okay.</i>


01:34:58.061 --> 01:34:59.858
<i>The barrier is pure energy.</i>


01:34:59.981 --> 01:35:01.778
<i>It's unbreachable.</i>


01:35:01.901 --> 01:35:03.619
<i>Yeah, I got that.</i>


01:35:04.781 --> 01:35:05.736
<i>Plan B.</i>


01:35:06.861 --> 01:35:08.852
<i>Sir, the Mark 7
is not ready for deployment.</i>


01:35:08.981 --> 01:35:11.131
Then skip the spinning rims.
We're on the clock.


01:35:30.062 --> 01:35:32.974
Please tell me you're going
to appeal to my humanity.


01:35:34.062 --> 01:35:36.337
Actually, I'm planning to threaten you.


01:35:36.462 --> 01:35:37.861
You should have left
your armour on for that.


01:35:37.982 --> 01:35:39.335
Yeah.


01:35:39.462 --> 01:35:40.497
It's seen a bit of mileage,


01:35:40.622 --> 01:35:43.136
and you've got
the glow stick of destiny.


01:35:43.902 --> 01:35:46.097
Would you like a drink?


01:35:46.222 --> 01:35:47.291
Stalling me won't change anything.


01:35:47.422 --> 01:35:49.458
No, no. Threatening.


01:35:49.582 --> 01:35:50.901
No drink? Are you sure?


01:35:51.022 --> 01:35:52.501
I'm having one.


01:35:53.502 --> 01:35:57.256
The Chitauri are coming.
Nothing will change that.


01:35:58.102 --> 01:35:59.455
What have I to fear?


01:35:59.582 --> 01:36:01.220
The Avengers.


01:36:03.222 --> 01:36:05.452
That's what we call ourselves.
We're sort of like a team.


01:36:05.582 --> 01:36:07.140
"Earth's mightiest heroes"-type thing.


01:36:07.262 --> 01:36:09.059
Yes, I've met them.


01:36:09.182 --> 01:36:10.171
Yeah.


01:36:10.302 --> 01:36:11.418
It takes us a while to get any traction,


01:36:11.543 --> 01:36:12.498
I'll give you that one.


01:36:12.623 --> 01:36:14.739
But let's do a head count, here.


01:36:14.863 --> 01:36:17.252
Your brother, the demigod,


01:36:18.903 --> 01:36:22.339
a super soldier, a living legend
who kind of lives up to the legend.


01:36:22.463 --> 01:36:25.500
A man with breathtaking
anger-management issues,


01:36:25.623 --> 01:36:28.581
a couple of master assassins,
and you, big fella,


01:36:29.183 --> 01:36:32.016
you've managed to piss off
every single one of them.


01:36:32.143 --> 01:36:33.098
That was the plan.


01:36:33.223 --> 01:36:35.134
Not a great plan.


01:36:35.263 --> 01:36:37.219
When they come,


01:36:37.343 --> 01:36:38.742
and they will,


01:36:38.863 --> 01:36:40.057
they'll come for you.


01:36:40.183 --> 01:36:41.138
I have an army.


01:36:41.263 --> 01:36:42.378
We have a Hulk.


01:36:42.863 --> 01:36:44.182
I thought the beast had wandered off.


01:36:44.303 --> 01:36:46.134
You're missing the point.
There is no throne.


01:36:46.263 --> 01:36:50.097
There is no version of this
where you come out on top.


01:36:50.223 --> 01:36:52.453
Maybe your army comes
and maybe it's too much for us,


01:36:52.583 --> 01:36:54.494
but it's all on you.


01:36:55.263 --> 01:36:56.298
Because if we can't protect the Earth,


01:36:56.463 --> 01:36:59.456
you can be damn well sure
we'll avenge it.


01:37:01.424 --> 01:37:04.336
How will your friends have time for me


01:37:04.464 --> 01:37:06.182
when they are so busy fighting you?


01:37:13.304 --> 01:37:14.293
This usually works.


01:37:14.424 --> 01:37:17.143
Well, performance issues,
it's not uncommon.


01:37:17.264 --> 01:37:19.095
One out of five...


01:37:20.504 --> 01:37:21.024
Jarvis, anytime now.


01:37:21.024 --> 01:37:23.299
Jarvis, anytime now.


01:37:24.984 --> 01:37:27.623
You will all fall before me.


01:37:27.744 --> 01:37:29.063
Deploy!


01:37:29.184 --> 01:37:30.537
Deploy!


01:37:56.625 --> 01:37:59.458
<i>And there's one other
person you pissed off.</i>


01:38:00.545 --> 01:38:01.739
<i>His name was Phil.</i>


01:38:24.545 --> 01:38:25.978
Right.


01:38:26.105 --> 01:38:27.299
Army.


01:39:36.707 --> 01:39:37.935
Loki!


01:39:38.067 --> 01:39:40.023
Turn off the Tesseract, or I'll destroy it.


01:39:40.147 --> 01:39:41.136
You can't.


01:39:41.267 --> 01:39:43.064
There is no stopping it.


01:39:43.187 --> 01:39:44.905
There is only


01:39:45.027 --> 01:39:46.096
the war.


01:39:46.227 --> 01:39:47.296
So be it.


01:40:08.507 --> 01:40:10.180
<i>Stark, we're on your three,
headed northeast.</i>


01:40:10.308 --> 01:40:12.344
What? Did you stop for drive-through?


01:40:12.468 --> 01:40:14.106
Swing up Park. I'm going
to lay them out for you.


01:40:31.428 --> 01:40:32.702
<i>Sir, we have more incoming.</i>


01:40:32.828 --> 01:40:34.500
Fine. Let's keep them occupied.


01:40:41.108 --> 01:40:42.905
- Nat?
- I see him.


01:41:25.429 --> 01:41:27.545
We got to get back up there.


01:42:16.790 --> 01:42:18.382
Stark, are you seeing this?


01:42:19.110 --> 01:42:21.465
<i>Seeing. Still working on believing.</i>


01:42:21.590 --> 01:42:22.909
Where's Banner?
Has he shown up yet?


01:42:23.030 --> 01:42:24.019
<i>Banner?</i>


01:42:24.150 --> 01:42:25.139
Just keep me posted.


01:42:25.830 --> 01:42:27.900
<i>Jarvis, find me a soft spot.</i>


01:42:30.070 --> 01:42:31.868
Look at this!


01:42:31.991 --> 01:42:32.946
Look around you!


01:42:33.911 --> 01:42:37.620
You think this madness
will end with your rule?


01:42:37.751 --> 01:42:39.184
It's too late.


01:42:40.631 --> 01:42:41.825
It's too late to stop it.


01:42:41.951 --> 01:42:45.660
No. We can, together.


01:42:51.991 --> 01:42:54.027
Sentiment.


01:43:20.472 --> 01:43:22.906
We've got civilians
still trapped up here.


01:43:24.032 --> 01:43:24.987
Loki.


01:43:36.152 --> 01:43:37.870
They're fish in a barrel down there.


01:43:43.112 --> 01:43:44.989
We got this. It's good. Go.


01:43:45.112 --> 01:43:46.431
Do you think you can hold them off?


01:43:46.552 --> 01:43:47.507
Captain,


01:43:49.432 --> 01:43:52.151
it would be my genuine pleasure.


01:44:17.913 --> 01:44:19.551
Just like Budapest all over again.


01:44:20.153 --> 01:44:22.542
You and I remember Budapest
very differently.


01:44:38.033 --> 01:44:38.988
It's going to be an hour


01:44:39.113 --> 01:44:40.341
before they can
scramble the National Guard.


01:44:40.473 --> 01:44:42.191
National Guard?


01:44:43.113 --> 01:44:44.546
Does the army know
what's happening here?


01:44:44.793 --> 01:44:45.748
Do we?


01:44:46.913 --> 01:44:48.062
You need men in these buildings.


01:44:48.193 --> 01:44:49.626
There are people inside and
they're going to be running


01:44:49.753 --> 01:44:50.902
right into the line of fire.


01:44:51.033 --> 01:44:52.864
You take them to the basements
or through the subway.


01:44:52.993 --> 01:44:54.506
You keep them off the streets.


01:44:54.633 --> 01:44:57.148
I need a perimeter as far back as 39th.


01:44:57.274 --> 01:44:58.832
Why the hell
should I take orders from you?


01:45:12.314 --> 01:45:13.463
I need men in those buildings.


01:45:13.594 --> 01:45:15.585
Lead the people down
and away from the streets.


01:45:15.714 --> 01:45:18.182
We're going to set up a perimeter
all the way down to 39th Street.


01:45:28.154 --> 01:45:29.667
Well, we got its attention.


01:45:29.794 --> 01:45:31.591
<i>What the hell was step two?</i>


01:45:59.915 --> 01:46:00.870
What's the story upstairs?


01:46:00.995 --> 01:46:02.826
The power surrounding the Cube
is impenetrable.


01:46:02.955 --> 01:46:05.469
<i>Thor's right. We got
to deal with these guys.</i>


01:46:05.595 --> 01:46:07.153
- How do we do this?
- As a team.


01:46:07.275 --> 01:46:08.503
I have unfinished business with Loki.


01:46:09.035 --> 01:46:10.024
Yeah? Well, get in line.


01:46:10.155 --> 01:46:11.110
Save it.


01:46:11.235 --> 01:46:12.509
Loki's going to keep
this fight focused on us,


01:46:12.635 --> 01:46:13.624
and that's what we need.


01:46:13.755 --> 01:46:15.347
Without him,
these things could run wild.


01:46:15.475 --> 01:46:18.308
We got Stark up top.
He's going to need us to...


01:46:25.355 --> 01:46:28.984
So, this all seems horrible.


01:46:29.435 --> 01:46:30.505
I've seen worse.


01:46:31.036 --> 01:46:31.991
Sorry.


01:46:32.116 --> 01:46:34.676
No, we could use a little worse.


01:46:34.796 --> 01:46:37.105
<i>- Stark, we got him.
- Banner?</i>


01:46:37.236 --> 01:46:38.430
Just like you said.


01:46:38.556 --> 01:46:41.150
Then tell him to suit up.
I'm bringing the party to you.


01:46:47.356 --> 01:46:49.347
I don't see how that's a party.


01:46:56.876 --> 01:46:57.831
Dr Banner.


01:46:59.516 --> 01:47:01.234
Now might be a really good
time for you to get angry.


01:47:02.236 --> 01:47:04.591
That's my secret, Captain.


01:47:06.236 --> 01:47:07.430
I'm always angry.


01:47:18.437 --> 01:47:19.995
<i>Hold on!</i>


01:47:48.677 --> 01:47:50.156
Send the rest.


01:47:56.637 --> 01:47:57.831
Guys.


01:47:57.957 --> 01:47:59.106
<i>Call it, Captain.</i>


01:47:59.237 --> 01:48:00.352
All right, listen up.


01:48:00.477 --> 01:48:03.150
Until we can close that portal,
our priority is containment.


01:48:03.277 --> 01:48:04.551
Barton, I want you on that roof.


01:48:04.677 --> 01:48:06.475
Eyes on everything.
Call out patterns and strays.


01:48:06.598 --> 01:48:07.917
Stark, you got the perimeter.


01:48:08.038 --> 01:48:09.153
Anything gets
more than three blocks out,


01:48:09.278 --> 01:48:10.757
you turn it back or you turn it to ash.


01:48:10.878 --> 01:48:12.027
<i>- Can you give me a lift?
- Right.</i>


01:48:12.158 --> 01:48:13.193
<i>Better clench up, Legolas.</i>


01:48:16.638 --> 01:48:18.913
Thor, you got to try
and bottleneck that portal.


01:48:19.038 --> 01:48:20.153
Slow them down.


01:48:20.278 --> 01:48:22.348
You got the lightning.
Light the bastards up.


01:48:24.558 --> 01:48:26.116
You and me,
we stay here on the ground.


01:48:26.238 --> 01:48:27.227
We keep the fighting here.


01:48:27.358 --> 01:48:28.313
And Hulk...


01:48:30.918 --> 01:48:31.953
Smash.


01:49:23.359 --> 01:49:24.428
Sir.


01:49:25.439 --> 01:49:26.394
The Council is on.


01:49:31.079 --> 01:49:34.196
Stark, you got a lot of strays
sniffing your tail.


01:49:35.959 --> 01:49:37.915
I'm just trying to keep them
off the streets.


01:49:38.039 --> 01:49:40.189
Well, they can't bank worth a damn.


01:49:40.319 --> 01:49:41.435
So find a tight corner.


01:49:41.560 --> 01:49:42.834
I will roger that.


01:50:04.880 --> 01:50:05.995
Oh, boy.


01:50:12.720 --> 01:50:14.278
Nice call.


01:50:14.400 --> 01:50:15.549
What else you got?


01:50:15.680 --> 01:50:18.353
<i>Thor is taking on
a squadron down on Sixth.</i>


01:50:18.480 --> 01:50:20.596
And he didn't invite me.


01:50:58.481 --> 01:51:00.039
Captain, none of this
is going to mean a damn thing


01:51:00.161 --> 01:51:01.355
if we don't close that portal.


01:51:01.481 --> 01:51:03.073
Our biggest guns couldn't touch it.


01:51:03.201 --> 01:51:05.351
Well, maybe it's not about guns.


01:51:07.201 --> 01:51:09.078
If you want to get up there,
you're going to need a ride.


01:51:10.121 --> 01:51:11.156
I got a ride.


01:51:12.241 --> 01:51:13.230
I could use a boost, though.


01:51:15.721 --> 01:51:16.677
Are you sure about this?


01:51:17.122 --> 01:51:19.556
Yeah. It's gonna be fun.


01:51:45.482 --> 01:51:47.279
Okay, turn, turn.


01:51:47.402 --> 01:51:49.074
Less! Less!


01:53:08.404 --> 01:53:11.237
<i>Captain, the bank
on 42nd past Madison.</i>


01:53:11.364 --> 01:53:13.036
<i>They've cornered
a lot of civilians in there.</i>


01:53:13.164 --> 01:53:14.995
I'm on it.


01:53:34.284 --> 01:53:36.002
Everyone! Clear out!


01:54:04.685 --> 01:54:06.277
<i>Director Fury,</i>


01:54:06.405 --> 01:54:08.123
<i>the Council has made a decision.</i>


01:54:08.245 --> 01:54:10.884
I recognise the Council
has made a decision.


01:54:11.005 --> 01:54:12.518
But given that
it's a stupid-ass decision,


01:54:12.645 --> 01:54:13.998
I have elected to ignore it.


01:54:14.125 --> 01:54:17.322
<i>Director, you're closer
than any of our subs.</i>


01:54:17.445 --> 01:54:18.400
<i>You scramble that jet...</i>


01:54:18.525 --> 01:54:21.119
That is the island of Manhattan,
Councilman.


01:54:21.245 --> 01:54:23.236
Until I'm certain my team can't hold it,


01:54:23.365 --> 01:54:25.242
I will not order a nuclear strike


01:54:25.405 --> 01:54:26.759
against a civilian population.


01:54:26.886 --> 01:54:29.195
<i>If we don't hold them here,
we lose everything.</i>


01:54:29.326 --> 01:54:31.965
If I send that bird out, we already have.


01:54:35.566 --> 01:54:37.204
You.


01:54:39.366 --> 01:54:40.481
Hawkeye!


01:54:41.886 --> 01:54:42.841
Nat, what are you doing?


01:54:43.726 --> 01:54:44.681
A little help?


01:54:49.766 --> 01:54:50.721
I got him.


01:55:16.207 --> 01:55:17.162
Enough!


01:55:17.487 --> 01:55:19.842
You are, all of you, beneath me!


01:55:19.967 --> 01:55:22.606
I am a god, you dull creature.


01:55:22.727 --> 01:55:24.160
And I will not be bullied by...


01:55:33.607 --> 01:55:35.404
Puny god.


01:55:43.207 --> 01:55:44.606
The sceptre...


01:55:45.727 --> 01:55:46.876
Doctor.


01:55:48.687 --> 01:55:51.406
Loki's sceptre. The energy.


01:55:51.527 --> 01:55:53.119
The Tesseract can't fight,


01:55:53.247 --> 01:55:55.203
but you can't protect against yourself.


01:55:55.327 --> 01:55:56.282
It's not your fault.


01:55:56.407 --> 01:55:57.601
You didn't know what you were doing.


01:56:00.527 --> 01:56:02.598
Actually, I think I did.


01:56:02.728 --> 01:56:05.561
I built in a safety
to cut their power source.


01:56:06.728 --> 01:56:08.081
Loki's sceptre.


01:56:08.208 --> 01:56:10.676
It may be able to close the portal.


01:56:12.688 --> 01:56:14.758
And I'm looking right at it.


01:56:26.248 --> 01:56:29.957
<i>Sir, we will lose power
before we penetrate that shell.</i>


01:56:36.328 --> 01:56:39.479
Jarvis, you ever hear the tale of Jonah?


01:56:39.608 --> 01:56:41.883
<i>I wouldn't consider him a role model.</i>


01:57:48.650 --> 01:57:50.368
<i>Director Fury is no longer in command.</i>


01:57:50.490 --> 01:57:52.446
<i>Override order 7-Alpha- 1- 1.</i>


01:57:52.570 --> 01:57:55.038
<i>7- Alpha- 1- 1, confirmed.
We're go for takeoff.</i>


01:57:55.890 --> 01:57:57.881
Sir, we have a bird in motion!


01:57:58.370 --> 01:58:00.281
Anyone on the deck,
we have a rogue bird.


01:58:00.410 --> 01:58:01.638
We need to shut it down!


01:58:01.770 --> 01:58:03.886
Repeat, takeoff is not authorised.


01:58:33.171 --> 01:58:35.241
Stark, do you hear me?


01:58:35.371 --> 01:58:37.407
You have a missile
headed straight for the city.


01:58:37.931 --> 01:58:39.250
<i>How long?</i>


01:58:39.371 --> 01:58:41.362
<i>Three minutes, max.</i>


01:58:41.491 --> 01:58:43.049
<i>The payload will wipe out Midtown.</i>


01:58:43.171 --> 01:58:45.127
Jarvis, put everything we got
into the thrusters.


01:58:45.251 --> 01:58:46.843
<i>I just did.</i>


01:58:59.211 --> 01:59:00.485
<i>Package is sent.</i>


01:59:00.611 --> 01:59:03.603
<i>Detonation in
2 minutes, 30 seconds, mark.</i>


01:59:25.452 --> 01:59:27.727
Are you ready for another bout?


01:59:28.372 --> 01:59:29.361
What, are you getting sleepy?


01:59:34.732 --> 01:59:36.404
Right at the crown!


01:59:42.172 --> 01:59:43.890
I can close it.


01:59:44.012 --> 01:59:45.968
Can anybody copy?


01:59:46.092 --> 01:59:47.161
I can shut the portal down.


01:59:47.292 --> 01:59:49.248
<i>- Do it!
- No, wait.</i>


01:59:49.372 --> 01:59:50.566
Stark, these things are still coming.


01:59:50.692 --> 01:59:51.647
I got a nuke coming in.


01:59:51.772 --> 01:59:53.603
It's gonna blow in less than a minute.


02:00:02.893 --> 02:00:04.645
And I know just where to put it.


02:00:11.533 --> 02:00:13.808
<i>Stark, you know that's a one-way trip.</i>


02:00:13.933 --> 02:00:15.252
Save the rest for the turn, J.


02:00:15.373 --> 02:00:19.286
<i>Sir, shall I try Miss Potts?</i>


02:00:19.413 --> 02:00:21.369
Might as well.


02:00:23.213 --> 02:00:25.488
<i>The streets of New York City
have become a battleground.</i>


02:00:25.613 --> 02:00:28.207
<i>The Army is here trying
to contain the violence</i>


02:00:28.333 --> 02:00:29.732
<i>but clearly, it is outmatched.</i>


02:00:29.853 --> 02:00:32.048
<i>And I have to say,
in all my years of reporting,</i>


02:00:32.173 --> 02:00:34.971
<i>I have never seen anything like this.</i>


02:00:35.093 --> 02:00:36.526
<i>We have limited information
on the team</i>


02:00:36.653 --> 02:00:40.248
<i>but we do know that
billionaire Tony Stark's Iron Man...</i>


02:01:50.575 --> 02:01:52.327
Come on, Stark.


02:01:58.695 --> 02:01:59.764
Close it.


02:02:19.015 --> 02:02:19.970
Son of a gun.


02:02:24.536 --> 02:02:26.094
He's not slowing down.


02:02:43.416 --> 02:02:44.815
Is he breathing?


02:03:11.537 --> 02:03:12.890
What the hell?


02:03:15.497 --> 02:03:17.533
What just happened?


02:03:17.657 --> 02:03:19.852
Please tell me nobody kissed me.


02:03:23.977 --> 02:03:25.569
We won.


02:03:27.817 --> 02:03:29.045
All right, yay!


02:03:29.177 --> 02:03:31.054
Hurray. Good job, guys.


02:03:31.177 --> 02:03:34.249
Let's just not come in tomorrow.
Let's just take a day.


02:03:35.097 --> 02:03:36.610
Have you ever tried shawarma?


02:03:37.017 --> 02:03:39.212
There's a shawarma joint
about two blocks from here.


02:03:39.337 --> 02:03:40.929
I don't know what it is,
but I want to try it.


02:03:41.337 --> 02:03:42.736
We're not finished yet.


02:03:47.497 --> 02:03:49.533
And then shawarma after.


02:04:10.298 --> 02:04:12.448
If it's all the same to you,


02:04:15.618 --> 02:04:17.210
I'll have that drink now.


02:04:24.778 --> 02:04:26.734
<i>Despite the devastation
of what has been confirmed</i>


02:04:26.858 --> 02:04:28.496
<i>as an extraterrestrial attack,</i>


02:04:28.618 --> 02:04:30.097
<i>the extraordinary heroics</i>


02:04:30.218 --> 02:04:32.095
<i>of the group known as the Avengers</i>


02:04:32.218 --> 02:04:33.697
<i>has been to many a cause
not only for comfort,</i>


02:04:33.818 --> 02:04:34.773
<i>but for celebration.</i>


02:04:34.898 --> 02:04:37.207
<i>It's just really great knowing
they're out there.</i>


02:04:37.338 --> 02:04:39.056
<i>That someone is watching over us.</i>


02:04:39.178 --> 02:04:40.327
<i>I love you, Thor!</i>


02:04:40.458 --> 02:04:42.096
<i>And then these guys were like...</i>


02:04:42.218 --> 02:04:43.492
<i>And then the air goes...</i>


02:04:43.618 --> 02:04:44.937
<i>And this green guy walks up
and he goes...</i>


02:04:45.058 --> 02:04:46.048
<i>I don't know.</i>


02:04:46.179 --> 02:04:48.534
<i>I don't exactly feel safer
with those things out there.</i>


02:04:48.659 --> 02:04:51.617
<i>It just seems that there's
a lot they're not telling us.</i>


02:04:51.739 --> 02:04:55.015
<i>Superheroes in New York?
Give me a break.</i>


02:04:55.139 --> 02:04:56.970
<i>These so-called "heroes"</i>


02:04:57.099 --> 02:04:58.327
<i>have to be held responsible</i>


02:04:58.459 --> 02:05:00.529
<i>for the destruction done to this city.</i>


02:05:00.659 --> 02:05:02.695
<i>This was their fight.
Where are they now?</i>


02:05:02.819 --> 02:05:03.299
<i>Tough questions are being asked
about the Avengers themselves.</i>


02:05:03.299 --> 02:05:05.529
<i>Tough questions are being asked
about the Avengers themselves.</i>


02:05:05.659 --> 02:05:06.614
<i>Their sudden appearance</i>


02:05:06.739 --> 02:05:08.058
<i>and equally sudden disappearance...</i>


02:05:08.179 --> 02:05:10.852
<i>What, this is all somehow their fault?</i>


02:05:12.819 --> 02:05:15.856
<i>Captain America saved my life.</i>


02:05:17.899 --> 02:05:21.255
<i>Wherever he is, and
wherever any of them are,</i>


02:05:21.379 --> 02:05:22.812
<i>I would just...</i>


02:05:23.579 --> 02:05:25.774
<i>I would want to say thank you.</i>


02:05:28.139 --> 02:05:29.572
<i>Where are the Avengers?</i>


02:05:29.699 --> 02:05:32.008
I'm not currently
tracking their whereabouts.


02:05:32.139 --> 02:05:34.210
I'd say they've earned
a leave of absence.


02:05:34.340 --> 02:05:35.853
<i>And the Tesseract?</i>


02:05:35.980 --> 02:05:38.130
<i>The Tesseract is where it belongs.</i>


02:05:38.540 --> 02:05:40.770
<i>Out of our reach.</i>


02:05:40.900 --> 02:05:42.379
<i>That's not your call.</i>


02:05:42.500 --> 02:05:43.489
I didn't make it.


02:05:43.620 --> 02:05:45.770
I just didn't argue with the god that did.


02:05:45.900 --> 02:05:47.618
<i>So, you let him take it</i>


02:05:47.740 --> 02:05:49.298
<i>and the war criminal, Loki,</i>


02:05:49.420 --> 02:05:51.058
<i>who should be
answering for his crime.</i>


02:05:51.180 --> 02:05:53.648
<i>I think he will be.</i>


02:06:06.580 --> 02:06:09.140
<i>I don't think you understand
what you've started,</i>


02:06:09.260 --> 02:06:11.615
<i>letting the Avengers
loose on this world.</i>


02:06:12.140 --> 02:06:13.095
<i>They're dangerous.</i>


02:06:13.220 --> 02:06:16.735
<i>They surely are,
and the whole world knows it.</i>


02:06:17.260 --> 02:06:19.728
Every world knows it.


02:06:20.140 --> 02:06:22.132
<i>Was that the point of all this?</i>


02:06:22.261 --> 02:06:23.933
<i>A statement?</i>


02:06:26.541 --> 02:06:27.940
<i>A promise.</i>


02:06:36.301 --> 02:06:37.780
<i>Sir, how does it work now?</i>


02:06:38.861 --> 02:06:40.772
They've gone their separate ways.


02:06:40.901 --> 02:06:43.699
Some, pretty extremely far.


02:06:44.421 --> 02:06:46.252
If we get into a situation like this again,


02:06:46.381 --> 02:06:47.860
what happens then?


02:06:47.981 --> 02:06:48.936
They'll come back.


02:06:50.381 --> 02:06:52.019
Are you really sure about that?


02:06:52.141 --> 02:06:53.096
I am.


02:06:54.661 --> 02:06:55.810
Why?


02:06:56.821 --> 02:06:58.937
Because we'll need them to.


02:09:43.505 --> 02:09:45.894
Humans.


02:09:47.145 --> 02:09:51.297
They are not the cowering
wretches we were promised.


02:09:52.225 --> 02:09:54.295
They stand.


02:09:55.105 --> 02:10:01.294
They are unruly,
and therefore cannot be ruled.


02:10:07.985 --> 02:10:10.738
To challenge them


02:10:10.865 --> 02:10:14.414
is to court death.


02:10:24.416 --> 02:10:30.416
<b>@ www.subs4free.com</b>

